<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0030/#screen-protocol-1-0> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Pooled siRNA targeting human kinome and Rho family GTPases/GEFs/GAPs in MCF10A breast myoepithelial cells stained for YAP/TAZ, F-actin, CD44" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000253 ;
    schema1:name "spinning disk confocal microscopy" .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0030/#screen-protocol-1-1> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "MCF10A cells obtained from ATCC were cultured in DMEM:F12 (GIBCO) containing 5% heat-inactivated fetal bovine serum (HI-FBS; GIBCO), 20 ng/ml EGF (Sigma), 10 μg/ml insulin (Sigma), 0.5 μg/ml hydrocortisone (Sigma) and 100 ng/ml cholera toxin (Sigma) at 37°C and 5% CO2, and cells used between passages 3 and 8.\"" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0003789> ;
    schema1:name "growth protocol" .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0030/#screen-protocol-1-2> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "\"MCF10A cells were reverse-transfected with Dharmacon siGenome pooled siRNA (Lipofectamine RNAiMAX, 40 ng siRNA/well). All siRNA-contaning wells and a subset of mock-transfected wells were seeded with 600 cells/well. Each plate also contained mock-transfected wells seeded with 450, 300, or 150 cells/well. Cells were cultured for 72 hours in DMEM:F12 plus EGF, insulin, hydrocortisone, cholera toxin, 5% heat-inactivated bovine serum. Fixed in 4% formaldehyde (PBS).\"" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007571> ;
    schema1:name "HCS library protocol" .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0030/#screen-protocol-1-3> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "\"Image acquisition was performed using Opera Cell::Explorer automated spinning disk confocal microscopes. Screens were performed using a 20X air objective lens (NA = 0.45) (PerkinElmer) and 30 fields of view (checkerboard pattern) were imaged in each well. Cells were stained with Hoechst (Channel 1), mouse anti-YAP/TAZ plus Alexa488 anti-mouse (Channel 2), Alexa647 phalloidin (Channel 3), rabbit anti-YAP/TAZ (C-term epitope) OR anti-CD44 plus Alexa568 anti-rabbit (Channel 4).\"" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007572> ;
    schema1:name "HCS image acquistion and feature extraction protocol" .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0030/#screen-protocol-1-4> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "\"Automated segmentation was performed using Acapella (PerkinElmer). Nuclei were segmented using the Hoechst channel and the  “nucleus region” was eroded by one pixel in order to compensate for segmentation errors. Predicted YAP/TAZ ratios (nuclear/perinuclear fluorescence intensity) were determined from morphologically diverse mock-transfected control cells by multiparametric linear regression using six shape features (cell area, nucleus area, neighbor fraction, local cell density, protrusion area, protrusion extent). Regression equations were applied to each single cell and the difference between observed and predicted YAP/TAZ ratios were determined to \"\"normalize\"\" YAP/TAZ localization for differences in cell shape. The average difference for each well was used to score hits. Note: ten-fold differences in total YAP/TAZ intensity were observed across the screen. \"\"High YAP/TAZ ratio\"\" does not necessarily correspond to target gene expression where total protein levels are low." ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007573> ;
    schema1:name "HCS data analysis protocol" .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0030/#total-dataset-size> a schema1:QuantitativeValue ;
    schema1:description "0.14 TB" ;
    schema1:unitCode "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000233" ;
    schema1:unitText "bytes" ;
    schema1:value 153931627888 .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0032/> a schema1:Dataset ;
    dwciri:measurementMethod obo:FBbi_00000246,
        <https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0032/#experiment-protocol-1-0>,
        <https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0032/#experiment-protocol-1-1>,
        <https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0032/#experiment-protocol-1-2>,
        <https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0032/#experiment-protocol-1-3> ;
    schema1:about obo:NCBITaxon_3702,
        <https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0032/#experiment-biosample-1> ;
    schema1:author <https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0032/#person-1> ;
    schema1:copyrightNotice "Yang et al, CC-BY-4.0, 2017" ;
    schema1:datePublished "2017-01-18" ;
    schema1:description "The cell walls of the shoot apical meristem (SAM), containing the stem cell niche that gives rise to the above-ground tissues, are crucially involved in regulating differentiation. It is currently unknown how these walls are built and refined or their role, if any, in influencing meristem developmental dynamics. We have combined polysaccharide linkage analysis, immuno-labeling, and transcriptome profiling of the SAM to provide a spatiotemporal plan of the walls of this dynamic structure. We find that meristematic cells express only a core subset of 152 genes encoding cell wall glycosyltransferases (GTs). Systemic localization of all these GT mRNAs by in situ hybridization reveals members with either enrichment in or specificity to apical subdomains such as emerging flower primordia, and a large class with high expression in dividing cells. The highly localized and coordinated expression of GTs in the SAM suggests distinct wall properties of meristematic cells and specific differences between newly forming walls and their mature descendants. Functional analysis demonstrates that a subset of CSLD genes is essential for proper meristem maintenance, confirming the key role of walls in developmental pathways." ;
    schema1:identifier "idr0032" ;
    schema1:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    schema1:name "Regulation of Meristem Morphogenesis by Cell Wall Synthases in Arabidopsis." ;
    schema1:publisher <https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/> ;
    schema1:size <https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0032/#file-count> ;
    schema1:thumbnailUrl "https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/webgateway/render_thumbnail/3125701/" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2016.04.026> .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0032/#experiment-biosample-1> a schema1:BioSample ;
    schema1:description "We performed systematic RNA in situ hybridization assays to examine the expression patterns of the SAM-expressed GTs at single-cell spatial resolution, including those transcripts that show either relative increases, reductions, or no change between SAM and flower samples." ;
    schema1:name "tissue" ;
    schema1:taxonomicRange obo:NCBITaxon_3702 .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0032/#experiment-protocol-1-0> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "We performed systematic RNA in situ hybridization assays to examine the expression patterns of the SAM-expressed GTs at single-cell spatial resolution, including those transcripts that show either relative increases, reductions, or no change between SAM and flower samples." ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246 ;
    schema1:name "fluorescence microscopy" .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0032/#experiment-protocol-1-1> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "\"RNA In Situ Hybridization of Wax-Embedded SAM Sections. For generation of gene-specific probes, cDNA fragments corresponding to each GT gene were amplified using gene-specific primers (Table S3) and ligated into the pGEM-T Easy vector (Promega). The constructs were verified by sequencing and then used as templates for in vitro transcription using the DIG RNA labeling kit (Roche). Shoot apices of Arabidopsis wild-type Col-0 or clv3-9 (a gift from Rudiger Simon, Heinrich Heine University) were fixed in FAA (formaldehyde, acetic acid, ethanol), embedded in wax, and cut into 8-mm sections. The sections were processed as described (http://www.its.caltech.edu/~7Eplantlab/protocols/insitu.pdf). In brief, after dewaxing, rehydration, and dehydration, the sections were hybridized with gene-specific probes and then incubated with anti-digoxigenin antibody (Roche).\"" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0003969> ;
    schema1:name "treatment protocol" .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0032/#experiment-protocol-1-2> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Signals were detected by the color reaction after application of NBT/BCIP (nitro blue tetrazo- lium/5-bromo-4-chloro-3-indolyl-phosphate; Roche)." ;
    schema1:name "image aquistion and feature extraction protocol" .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0032/#experiment-protocol-1-3> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "\"Based on the expression pattern, genes were divided into five categories.\"" ;
    schema1:name "data analysis protocol" .

