<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0072/#screen-protocol-1-0> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "EGFP fusion proteins of organelle marker proteins were stably expressed in eukaryotic cells MCF10A." ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246 ;
    schema1:name "fluorescence microscopy" .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0072/#screen-protocol-1-1> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "MCF10A were cultured in DMEM/F12 (Gibco) supplemented with 5% horse serum (Gibco), penicillin/streptomycin, 10 ug/ml insulin (Sigma), 0.02 ug/ml EGF (Preprotech), 0.5 ug/ml hydrocortisone (Sigma), and 0.25 mg/L isoproterenol (Sigma). All cell lines were maintained in a 5% CO2 atmosphere at 37oC.Cells were transduced with EGFP fusion organelle marker proteins. Prior to imaging cells were stained with DRAQ5 (50nM).Cells were imaged using PerkinElmer OPERA¨ QHS spinning disk automated confocal microscopes with 40x water objectives (NA =  0.9) in a defined temperature (37oC) and CO2 (5%) environment by using EvoShell acquisition software. Images were collected by using 3-Peltier-cooled 12-bit CCD cameras (Type sensiCam, PCO.imaging, Germany, camera resolution 1.3MPixel). Feature extraction was carried out by using Perkin Elmer Acapella software. Once images were acquired, they were segmented to obtain cell, nucleus and cytoplasm region.Features for all the different regions were acquired. Features are broadly classified into Shape, Texture, Colocalization and ROI features." ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0003789> ;
    schema1:name "growth protocol" .

