<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0078/#screen-protocol-1-0> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "primary screens (genome wide)" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000253 ;
    schema1:name "spinning disk confocal microscopy" .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0078/#screen-protocol-1-1> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Briefly, haploid mutant MATa strains expressing tagged FPs derived from SGA were grown and imaged in low fluorescence synthetic minimal medium64 supplemented with antibiotics and 2% glucose. Nonessential gene deletion mutants were grown and imaged in logarithmic phase at 30°C, and TS mutants of essential genes were first grown to mid-logarithmic phase and imaged at 26°C, and then incubated for three hours at 37°C and imaged at 37°C. Cells were transferred to a Concanavalin A (ConA) coated 384-well PerkinElmer CellCarrier Ultra imaging plate and centrifuged for 45 seconds at 500 rpm before imaging. To aid in cell segmentation, Dextran Alexa Fluor 647 (Molecular Probes) was added to cells in low fluorescence medium to a final concentration of 10 μg/ml before imaging." ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0003789> ;
    schema1:name "growth protocol" .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0078/#screen-protocol-1-2> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "For genome wide screens, micrographs were obtained on the Opera (PerkinElmer) automated spinning disk confocal microscope. Three fields with Z-stacks of 5 optical sections with 0.8 μm spacing were collected per well, with each field of view containing 50 - 150 cells. Secondary screens were imaged on an Opera Phenix (PerkinElmer) automated microscope. All imaging was done with a 60x water- immersion objective. Acquisition settings included using a 405/488/561/640 nm primary dichroic mirror. yEGFP was excited using a 488 nm laser, and emission collected through a 520/35 nm filter. tdTomato was excited using a 561 nm laser, and emission collected through a 600/40 nm filter. Dextran Alexa Fluor 647 was excited using a 640 nm laser, and emission collected through a 690/50 nm filter." ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0003969> ;
    schema1:name "treatment protocol" .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0078/#screen-protocol-1-3> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "See paper Methods section for full description." ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0007571> ;
    schema1:name "HCS library protocol" .

