    schema1:name "growth protocol" .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0098/#experiment-protocol-1-2> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "The abdominal skin of the mice was left untreated. The back skin of the mice were treated with an immunosupressant solution (100ug of Dimethylbenz[a]anthracene (DMBA) dissolved into 0.2mL of acetone) at the beginning of the experiment and a tumor promoter (25mg of 12-OTetradecanoylphorbol-13-acetate (TPA) in 100mL of ethanol) was applied every week" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0003969> ;
    schema1:name "treatment protocol" .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0098/#experiment-protocol-1-3> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "All images corresponding to normal tissue come from abdominal skin. Tissue from the back skin was classified as dysplasia if it looked inflamed, but not comming from warts. Tissue from wrats on the back skin was classified as papilloma. Tissue coming from warts bigger than 5mm on the back skin was classified as squamous cell carcinoma." ;
    schema1:name "image acquisition and feature extraction protocol" .

