<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0115/#experiment-protocol-1-1> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Cells were grown in high glucose DulbeccoÕs Modified EagleÕs Medium (DMEM) containing 4.5 g/l D-glucose (Sigma Aldrich, St. Louis, MO) supplemented with 10% fetal calf serum (FCS), 2 mM l-glutamine, 1 mM sodium pyruvate, and 100 _g/ml penicillin and streptomycin at 37 ¡C and 5% CO2." ;
    schema1:name "growth protocol" .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0115/#experiment-protocol-1-2> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "On the day of live-cell imaging, DMEM was replaced by imaging medium: CO2-independent medium without phenol red (Invitrogen) containing 20% FCS, 2 mM l-glutamine, and 100 _g/ml penicillin and streptomycin. The imaging medium was supplemented with 50 nM silicon-rhodamine (SiR) Hoechst." ;
    schema1:name "image acquisition and feature extraction protocol" .

<https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/study/idr0115/#experiment-protocol-1-3> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Cells were imaged in 3D using a confocal microscope (LSM780; Carl Zeiss, Oberkochen, Germany) and a 40_ 1.2 NA C-Apochromat water immersion objective (Carl Zeiss) at 37 ¡C in a microscope-body-enclosing incubator." ;
    schema1:name "data analysis protocol" .

