        <https://ssbd.riken.jp/repository/ssbd-repos-000236/#biosample-1> ;
    schema1:author <https://ssbd.riken.jp/repository/ssbd-repos-000236/#auth-001> ;
    schema1:datePublished "2022-06-30" ;
    schema1:description "We performed 3D timelapse imaging of 52 embryos, in which the cell membrane is labeled with green fluorescent protein (GFP), for two hours from the two-cell stage. An image restoration method based on deep learning was applied to improve the image quality. An image processing method called BCOMS (Biologically Constrained Optimization-based cell Membrane Segmentation) was applied and the cellular regions were segmented." ;
    schema1:identifier "ssbd-repos-000236" ;
    schema1:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    schema1:name "Cell membrane images, restored images, and segmentation results of 52 C. elegans embryos." ;
