<https://ssbd.riken.jp/v3/project/337-Isoe-BrainRegion#biosample-1> a schema1:BioSample ;
    schema1:description "The medaka brain deriverd from two transgenic lines. One is the transgenic line (Tg (HuC:loxp-DsRed-loxp-GFP)) that visualized neural progenitors by the HuC promoter. The second is a line (Tg (HSP-Cre)) that expresses Cre recombinase under the heat shock protein promoter. In the absence of the recombination, DsRed is expressed in the neural progenitor cells. When Cre-loxp recombination is induced the neural progenitors express GFP instead of DsRed." ;
    schema1:name "HuC:loxp-DsRed-loxp-GFP, HSP-Cre ~ neuron" ;
    schema1:taxonomicRange <https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/datasets/taxonomy/8090> .

