<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/EMPIAR-10365#c645b502-bebf-497a-8e97-5b9bdd222b6a> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Images were acquired with a ZEISS Merlin SEM at 1.8 keV landing energy, 270 pA beam current, and 0.8 ms dwell time. 2.5 TB comprising 11,416 slices with >200,000 image tiles were acquired at 10x10 nm2 pixel size and 25 nm cutting thickness. The open-source acquisition software SBEMimage was used over the seven-week-long acquisition. For image registration, translational offsets between neighboring image tiles were calculated using optimized normalized cross-correlation. Pairwise relative offsets between neighboring tiles were used to optimize tile positions in a global total least square displacement sense. Histograms of neighboring image tiles were matched to adjust contrast and brightness before in-plane stitching." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "ZEISS Merlin SEM with ATLAS 5 software" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000585 ;
    schema1:name "Serial Block-Face Scanning Electron Microscopy" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/EMPIAR-10365#e3392f0c-1325-4a09-bcc5-8c3ddebc6734> a schema1:BioSample ;
    schema1:description "6 days post-fertilization Platynereis dumerilii larvae from an established culture at EMBL Heidelberg. Animals were kept and raised in natural seawater, at a constant temperature of 18°C, and under a 16-8 hours light-dark cycle." ;
    schema1:name "Platynereis dumerilii larvae" ;
    schema1:taxonomicRange obo:NCBITaxon_6359 .

