<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/EMPIAR-11078#d3819b85-3429-4d70-ba05-d26ffa1da47c> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "EM grids with FIB-thinned cells were transferred to a 300 kV Titan Krios microscope (FEI, Thermo Fisher Scientific), equipped with a post-column energy filter (Gatan) and a K2 Summit direct detector camera (Gatan). Using SerialEM software, tilt-series were acquired from −60° to +60°, with 2° increments (bidirectional, separated at −0° or −20°). A subset was collected using a dose-symmetrical tilt scheme. Images were recorded in movie mode at 12 frames per second, with an object pixel size of 3.42 Å (magnification of 42,000x) and a defocus of −4 to −6 μm. The total accumulated dose for each tilt-series was ∼100 e−/Å2. Each tomogram was acquired from a separate cell and therefore can be considered a biological replicate. Several different cell cultures and >10 imaging sessions were used to produce the dataset of 20 tomograms." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "300 kV Titan Krios microscope (FEI, Thermo Fisher Scientific), equipped with a post-column energy filter (Gatan) and a K2 Summit direct detector camera (Gatan)." ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000256 ;
    schema1:name "Cryo-electron tomography" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/EMPIAR-11078#d820f8ae-ba23-444f-bf88-27bc5055c61b> a schema1:BioSample ;
    schema1:description "C. reinhardtii cells, obtained from the Chlamydomonas Resource Center (University of Minnesota, Minneapolis, MN USA). For in situ cryo-ET, we used strain CC-3994 (mat3-4 mt+). This strain has smaller cells, which is beneficial for vitrification during plunge freezing and also increases the chances of hitting a transition zone region by FIB milling. For cryo-ET of basal bodies following ciliary abscission, we used strain CC-4533 (cw15 mt-; Jonikas CMJ030). This strain lacks a cell wall and thus easily ruptures during blotting onto EM grids, enabling cryo-ET of basal bodies in thin ice without FIB milling." ;
    schema1:name "_:Chlamydomonas reinhardtii" ;
    schema1:taxonomicRange obo:NCBITaxon_3055 .

