<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/EMPIAR-12104#60829db3-985b-4832-ac12-639eb5d14412> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Cryo-electron tomograms were acquired on a Titan Krios microscope operated at 300 kV (Thermo Fisher Scientific) equipped with a field-emission gun, a quantum post-column energy filter (Gatan) and a K3 direct detector (Gatan). Data was collected in low-dose mode using automation scripts in SerialEM. Tilt series were acquired from -60° to +60° in 2° increments at a magnification of 26,000x with a calibrated pixel size of 3.425 Å, using a dose-symmetric tilt scheme, defocus range of 2-4 μm, and keeping the total accumulated dose below 150 e-/A2. 14 tilt series were acquired for the glucose control and 26 tilt series for the starvation condition. Prior to tomogram reconstruction, tilt movie frames were corrected for gain reference and beam-induced motion in Warp 1.0.9 alongside contrast transfer function (CTF) estimation. Tomograms were aligned and reconstructed by weighted back-projection in AreTomo at 4x binning, corresponding to a pixel size of 13.7 Å." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Titan Krios microscope operated at 300 kV (Thermo Fisher Scientific) equipped with a field-emission gun, a quantum post-column energy filter (Gatan) and a K3 direct detector (Gatan)" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000256 ;
    schema1:name "Cryo-electron tomography" .

