    schema1:description "Serial block-face scanning electron microscopy was performed using the Apreo Volume Scope (Thermo Fisher Scientific) with integrated microtome for alternating diamond knife cutting and SEM scanning. Scanning parameters: high vacuum mode, working distance 6.5 mm, 1.78 kV, 0.1 nA, 1-3 us pixel dwell time, T1 backscattering electron detector. Scan 1 was acquired in radial orientation at 25 x 25 x 50 nm voxel size, covering from cone outer segments to the scleral border of the inner plexiform layer." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Apreo Volume Scope (Thermo Fisher Scientific Inc., Brno, Czech Republic)" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000586 ;
    schema1:name "Apreo Volume Scope SBF-SEM acquisition" .

