    schema1:description "Cell monolayers were imaged on a CV7000 (Yokogawa) high content microscope, using a 10x N.A. 0.4 air objective objective. The 405 nm laser was used to image nuclei (Hoechst H33258), the 488 nm laser was used to image phospho-Ser807/811 Rb, the 561 nm laser was used to detect either p21 or p27 CDK inhibitory proteins (depending on the specific stain used) and the 647 nm laser was used to detect EdU. " ;
    schema1:labEquipment "CV7000 (Yokagawa) high content microscope in confocal mode (pinhole size of 50 um). Four fields of view were taken per well using a 10x air objective, NA 0.4. " ;
