<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1033#4b70ebfa-9cc3-477c-b652-d4a0a70716b1> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """The emission iris was closed to match the objective, according to the specifications by CREST Optics. The ring of the objective was adjusted to the thickness of the plate bottom. The camera used was a Photometrix BSI Express Back illuminated sCMOS for widefield images; Sensitivity 11 Bits mode, readout speed 200 MHz.
The α-actinin channel was acquired using a 546 nm laser and a Pentaband emission filter (441/30; 511/26; 593/37; 684/34; 817/66 nm). The laser power and exposure time were set to get the brightest possible images without any saturation. The same settings were used for all the samples to be compared.
The brightness and contrast of the analyzed images were adjusted to the same settings, and the images were acquired either in widefield as tiles (9x9).
""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "S Plan Fluor Ph2 ELWD 60x/0.70 objective on a Nikon Ti2 microscope equipped with a CREST Optics V3 spinning disk confocal (50 um pinholes). " ;
    schema1:name "Widefield images acquisition " .

