<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1043#35c60838-5b29-4867-b8dd-54aae7359d7f> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """we used 405 nm (DAPI Channel) or 488 nm (CENPC channel) excitation
lasers, a 405/488/561/640 nm excitation dichroic mirror, a 60X water objective (NA 1.2), 445/45
(DAPI Channel) or 525/50 nm (CENPC Channel) bandpass emission mirrors, and a 16-bit sCMOS
camera (2048 X 2048 pixels, binning 1X1, pixel size: 0.108 microns). Z-stacks of 14 microns were
acquired at 1 micron intervals and maximally projected on the fly. Images were acquired in 22
FOV per well.""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "CellVoyager CV7000/CV8000" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000253 ;
    schema1:name "Figure 4 Image acquisition" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1043#41240b84-07e8-44f2-8adc-8857f4375b66> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """For DNA FISH experiments, we used 405 nm (DAPI Channel), 561 nm (Probe A channel), or 640
nm (Probe B channel) excitation lasers. In addition, we used a 405/488/561/640 nm excitation
dichroic mirror, a 60X water objective (NA 1.2), and 445/45 nm (DAPI Channel), 600/37 nm
(Probe A channel), or 676/29 nm (Probe B channel) bandpass emission mirrors in front of a 16-bit
sCMOS camera (2048 X 2048 pixels, binning 1X1, pixel size: 0.108 microns). Z-stacks of 7
microns were acquired at 1 micron intervals and maximally projected on the fly. Images were
acquired in 32 fields of view (FOV) per well.""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "CellVoyager CV7000/CV8000" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000253 ;
    schema1:name "Figure 3 Image acquisition" .

