    schema1:description "We used a 488 nm excitation laser, a 405/488/561/640 nm excitation dichroic mirror, either a 40X air objective (NA 0.95) or a 40X water objective (NA 1.15), a 525/50 nm bandpass emission mirror, and a 16-bit sCMOS camera (2048 X 2048 pixels, binning 2X2, pixel size: 0.325 microns). Z-stacks of 0.5 microns were acquired at 100 sec intervals and maximally projected on the fly, every 100s for 10 hours." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "CellVoyager CV7000/CV8000" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000253 ;
    schema1:name "Figure 5 Image acquisition" .

