<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1044#4fc29909-41ff-4e35-99f5-e1fb90942904> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Fixed and mounted cells were imaged on the SP8 microscope using a scanning speed of 400 Hz, pinhole set to 1AU, and a white light laser power of 70%. For the blue channel, the 405 nm laser line was used at 15.7% output power, and the image was collected in the 420-466 nm range using a PMT (gain 631.5, offset 0).  For the green channel, the 487 nm laser line was used between 8.9-15.8% output power, and the image was collected in the 502-552 nm range using a HyD (gain 116.8, offset 0). For the infrared channel, the 647 nm laser line was used at 1.1% output power, and the image was collected in the 662-704 nm range using a HyD (gain 51.3, offset 0)." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Leica SP8 inverted confocal microscope equipped with a 63x, 1.4 NA PlanApo oil immersion objective and one PMT and two HyD detectors. A white light laser in conjunction with an acousto-optic tunable filter (AOTF; Leica) was used for illumination." ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000251 ;
    schema1:name "Confocal Microscopy" .

