<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1071#5bd91f84-3777-4c87-aafd-11dd7b81c155> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Eligible participants for this study were patients aged 18 and older who received high-resolution flat-panel CT (DynaCT; Siemens, Erlangen, Germany) without intravenous contrast for otologic evaluations at the Johns Hopkins Hospital from January 2018 to December 2019. CT scans with significant artifacts or structural alterations precluding accurate measurements, including advanced otosclerosis, labyrinthitis ossificans, or fractures, were excluded. At our institution, flat panel CT is primarily used to investigate potential dehiscences in the superior semicircular canal (SSC) but is increasingly used for other indications. The study aimed to include a sample of 50 control ears without a radiologic diagnosis of superior canal dehiscence (SCD) and 50 ears with SCD based on radiology reports." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Flat-panel CT imaging" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00001005 ;
    schema1:name "Supplementary Digital Content 5 for Superior Canal Dehiscence and the Risk of Additional Dehiscences: A Retrospective CT Cohort Study (Shankar et al.): Image Acquisition" .

