<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1083#afafb0de-7027-4c41-bda7-42e0a8732330> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """At the indicated tissue age or experimental time point, samples were washed at the basolateral side with HBSS and subsequently fixed by addition of 10% formalin to the apical and basal compartment, for 45 min at RT. Samples were washed once with HBSS containing 0.05% NaN3 and stored at 4°C in this buffer until further processing. The membranes were cut from the inserts and processed for ICC or histology. For ICC, the tissues were permeabilized for 20 min at RT with HBBS 0.5 % Triton. Then, washed once with HBSS with 0,05% NaN3 and stained with the respective primary and secondary antibodies and/or dyes (see key resource table). The samples were embedded in Mowiol and cured for >48 hours at RT before imaging. Image analysis and quantification was performed with Imaris Imaging Analysis Software or NIS-Elements General Analysis software.
For analysis of tissue attachment, samples were washed extensively with HBSS (5 min in shaking incubator and subsequent pipetting of buffer) prior to fixation. ICC samples were prepared and imaged as described above. Extracellular bacteria were segmented with ImageJ (Fiji) and the ‘Analyze particles’ function was used to count. For each conditions 17 images of three individual samples were acquired and analyzed (n>50). """ ;
    schema1:labEquipment "ICC samples were imaged with Olympus SpinD (CSU-W1) equipped with a Hamamatsu ORCA-Fusion (sCMOS) camera and UPL X APO 10x/0.4 or 30x/1.05 or UPLXAPO O 60x/1.42 objective or Nikon CSU-W1 equipped with an 2x Hamamatsu ORCA-Fusion camera (sCMOS) and CFP Plan Apo Lambda 100x/1.45 or CFP Plan Apo Lambda 10x/0.45 objective" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000251,
        obo:FBbi_00000345 ;
    schema1:name "Immunocytochemistry" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1083#b35d8f0c-23df-4f91-8d79-0b79ced4c734> a schema1:Person ;
    schema1:affiliation <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1083#a5306e8a-3370-4f5e-bc65-71657a2938a3> ;
    schema1:name "Rosmarie Sütterlin" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1083#be2eb1ae-8de5-4589-bf3b-4a3ffcd404b1> a schema1:Person ;
