    schema1:datePublished "2024-03-23" ;
    schema1:description "Here we provide the raw RNA-FISH images displayed in the study \"YY1 binding is a gene-intrinsic barrier to Xist-mediated gene silencing\". These images were collected from iXist-ChrX mouse embryonic stem cell lines engineered with the FKBP12 degron tag fused to endogenous YY1, such that addition of dTAG-13 acutely degrades YY1 protein from cells. Degradation of YY1 - either prior to Xist induction or after prolonged Xist induction - has little effect on the appearance of Xist RNA territories over the Xi chromosome. " ;
    schema1:identifier "S-BIAD1091" ;
    schema1:keywords "RNA-FISH",
        "X inactivation",
        "Xist",
        "YY1" ;
    schema1:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    schema1:name "RNA-FISH of Xist in iXist-ChrX mouse embryonic stem cells upon acute degradation of YY1" ;
