<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1092#7ebccd3c-5ed0-4ed0-9371-a846a1d76853> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """We used the black and white camera Axiocam 506 mono (D). For mosaic acquisitions (“tiles”) we used a tiling overlap of 8-10% and image tiles were not stitched. Images were magnified 5x and 10x (Fluar 5x/0.25 M27 and EC Plan-Neofluar 10x/0.3 Ph1 M27). Brightfield and fluorescence images of 13 mm² of co-culture were acquired every 15 minutes for 63 h. Movement speed of the motorized table was adjusted to the lowest setting that allows acquisition of the complete region within 15 minutes.
""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment """All microscopy equipment was acquired from ZEISS. The microscope was an Axio Observer 7 with confocal Apotome.2 equipped with a motorized reflector revolver and motorized scanning table (130x100 mm). The microscope was mounted on an Antivibrations-Set [Axio Observer (D)] with two antivibration carrier plates, each equipped with two vibration dampening feet. The light source was a microLED 2 for transmission light and (for fluorescence) Colibri 7 (R[G/Y]B-UV) for the green channel of incident light (590 nm). For excitation (EX) and emission (EM) light filtering and beam splitting (BS) we used the following reflector: 43 HE Cy 3 shift free (E) (EX: 550/25, BS: 570, EM: 605/70).
Live cells were imaged inside an ibidi Stage Top Incubation System equilibrated to 80% humidity, 5% CO2 and 37 °C.""" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000243,
        obo:FBbi_00000246,
        obo:FBbi_00000249 ;
    schema1:name "Automated Time-Lapse Microscopy" .

