<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1096#983b6366-a5c1-430c-8348-03688290f994> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "null" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "lensless imaging system.  It is composed of an imaging module and an illumination module. The imaging module is adapted from an fp L Interchangeable-lens Mirrorless Type Digital Camera (SIGMA, Aizu, Japan). The image sensor is a full frame (36.0 mm × 24.0 mm) back-illuminated Bayer CMOS sensor, with 62.4 million pixels: an array of 9 520 × 6 328 pixels at 3.8 µm pitch. We designed and manufactured the electronic system to operate this sensor. The Petri dish is set directly on the sensor and illuminated from above by the illumination module. That module consists of two monochromatic light sources coupled into a multimode optical fibre via a Y fiber SMA (Thorlabs BFY105LS02): a green LED (550 nm) Thorlabs MINTF4 and a near-infrared LED (940 nm) Thorlabs M940F3." ;
    schema1:name "lensless imaging" .

