<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1133#b8dfe291-8693-46db-8d01-36ccfb9e77b9> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """Relevant anatomical structures were identified in the nuclear DAPI field, and confocal images of connexin 43 as well as DAPI were collected in the photon-counting mode to minimise batch-to-batch variability; x40 magnification was used. Patients’ identities and disease status were coded, and researchers conducting the imaging were blinded to the experimental conditions. 
In the present dataset, snapshots of maximal intensity stack projections are shown in addition to the raw files.""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Leica Stellaris 8" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000251 ;
    schema1:name "Imaging of connexin 43 in the human brain" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1134> a schema1:Dataset ;
    dwciri:measurementMethod obo:FBbi_00000246,
        obo:FBbi_00000249,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1134#b64ae7e2-c038-4420-90a1-c87ed1647a66> ;
    schema1:about obo:NCBITaxon_9606,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1134#71db1d99-9928-476d-b1ff-ce3747d1fb20> ;
    schema1:author <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8579-4919>,
        <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2018-2986>,
        <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3956-9363> ;
    schema1:datePublished "2024-04-30" ;
    schema1:description """This dataset contains a 3D movie of an MCF10A acini. Three fluorescence channels encode a nuclear marker for segmentation and tracking, and reporters for CDK2 and ERK activity. 

Data dimensions: [t,c,z,y,x] -> [145, 3, 188, 188, 188]
Data format: zarr, 
Voxel size: 0.29x0.29x0.29 μm/px
Time resolution: 5min/frame

Channels:
C0: ERK-KTR-mTurquoise2 (ERK activity)
C1: DHB-mRuby2 (CDK2 activity)
C2: H2B-miRFP703 (nuclear marker)

The dataset is used in the paper accompanying conv-paint, an interactive image segmentation tool for napari. The paper will be linked as soon as a preprint is published. The dataset is an interesting test set for various image analysis tools, especially because of its high dimensionality. Stored as a zarr array, it can be drag-and-dropped into the image viewer napari for interactive visualisation and exploration. Each chunk represents one time point.""" ;
    schema1:identifier "S-BIAD1134" ;
    schema1:keywords "3d",
        "MCF10A",
        "fluorescence",
        "lightsheet",
        "organoid",
        "timelapse",
        "zarr" ;
    schema1:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    schema1:name "Light sheet 3D timelapse of a human breast cell acini" ;
    schema1:publisher <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/bioimage-archive/> ;
    schema1:size <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1134#1037e7dd-b10a-47a1-885c-1f3b2998ff1c>,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1134#480bb0bc-db43-46e5-88ae-071380b9d63c> .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1134#1037e7dd-b10a-47a1-885c-1f3b2998ff1c> a <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/QuantitiveValue> ;
    schema1:unitCode "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000189" ;
    schema1:unitText "file count" ;
    schema1:value 145 .

