<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1154#483a864e-7cbb-4464-8d33-883a02eb83c0> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """FCA-mScarletI-I was excited with a 561 nm laser. The fluorescence emission arrived at the detector after passing through a filter that allowed wavelengths between 495-550 nm and above 570 nm to pass through.
FCA-mTurquoise and FLL2-EYFP were excited at 458 (mTurquoise) and 514 nm (eYFP). The fluorescence emission of the samples passed through a filter that only allowed wavelengths in the 465-505 nm range and above 525 nm to reach the Airyscan detector, which was operating in super resolution mode.
FCA-mScarlet-I and FLC-lacO-lacI-eYFP were acquired on a Zeiss LSM980 using LD C-Apochromat 40x/NA 1.1 water-immersion objective. The fluorescent probes, eYFP and mScarlet-I, were excited at 488 and 561 nm,""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Confocal images were acquired on a Zeiss LSM 880 or Zeiss LSM 980 upright microscope equipped with an Airyscan detector and a C-Apochromat 63x/NA 1.2 water-immersion objective or LD C-Apochromat 40x/NA 1.1 water-immersion objective." ;
    schema1:name "Image acquisition of FCA condensates" .

