<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1159#eba77a84-4374-4bc6-88a1-6fc958d0b9f1> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "For imaging, zebrafish were embedded in low-melting-point agarose in an 8-well Ibidi µ-slide, adding water on top for proper hydration. An inverted widefield microscope, with an objective that has a long working distance, was used for imaging. Up to 4 Ibidi slides were placed into the slide holder in the widefield microscope. The brightfield and all required fluorescence channels, e.g., GFP (excitation at 475 nm & emission 520 nm), and mCherry (excitation at 555 nm & emission at 605 nm) were set up. The positions of all otic vesicles were set with a 20X objective that has a long working distance (minimum 1 mm) and all zebrafish were imaged within the brightfield and fluorescence channels." ;
