<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1200#1f2527f1-e93c-420d-878f-62dc214e190c> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Each fish was imaged at approximately the same horizontal plane referenced from the dorsal surface of the tectum continuously for 2 to 10 minutes under the same laser power (10mW, 99.21 w/cm^2at the sample). Imaging data was collected at 33-50 frames per second (fps) for each single channel." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Calcium imaging was performed on a custom-built light sheet microscope. The system is a modified version of the OpenSPIM setup (Pitrone et al. (2013) OpenSPIM: an open-access light-sheet microscopy platform. Nat Meth 10:598-599), as described in our previous work (Liu et al., (2019) Imaging neural events in zebrafish larvae with linear structured illumination light sheet fluorescence microscopy. Neurophotonics 6:015009.).  The microscope is controlled through a custom-written LabVIEW program using a Dell Precision 5810 Tower with 32GB RAM and a quad-core Intel(R) Xeon(R) E5-1603 v3 processor. " ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246 ;
    schema1:name "Image Acquisition" .

