<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1203#9f4170d8-5753-42fa-a2e9-666a21b21870> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """Nikon AX-R confocal microscope with a CFI Apochromat LWD Lambda S 20XC WI objective (0.95 NA) (Nikon). Time-lapse images were captured using a CFI Plan Apochromat Lambda D 20X objective (0.80 NA) (Nikon). 
Cells were kept in a precise incubation system (STXG-WSKMX-SET, TOKAI HIT) at 37 ºC in a humidified atmosphere 5% CO2.
Galvano scanner, images were acquired every 30 min for 48 h.
Resonant scanner, images were acquired every 10 min for 48 h (289 images - Figure 4A-B), every 20 min for 48 h (145 images - Figure 5A and), or every 5 min for 24 h (289 images - Figure 5B). 
Microscopy and image acquisition were performed using NIS-Elements (Nikon). A high-content imaging system, JOBS (Nikon), was utilized to automatically scan the 384-well plates.""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment """Nikon AX-R confocal microscope with a CFI Apochromat LWD Lambda S 20XC WI objective (0.95 NA) (Nikon). Time-lapse images were captured using a CFI Plan Apochromat Lambda D 20X objective (0.80 NA) (Nikon). 
Cells were kept in a precise incubation system (STXG-WSKMX-SET, TOKAI HIT) at 37 ºC in a humidified atmosphere 5% CO2.
Galvano scanner, images were acquired every 30 min for 48 h.
Resonant scanner, images were acquired every 10 min for 48 h (289 images - Figure 4A-B), every 20 min for 48 h (145 images - Figure 5A and), or every 5 min for 24 h (289 images - Figure 5B). 
Microscopy and image acquisition were performed using NIS-Elements (Nikon). A high-content imaging system, JOBS (Nikon), was utilized to automatically scan the 384-well plates.""" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000251 ;
    schema1:name "EMBOR-2024-59195 - Robust tissue pattern formation by coupling morphogen signal and cell adhesion" .

