<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1235#b21fe318-3f6b-41ce-a4d8-057359ced6c1> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """Samples were imaged in a Talos 120 transmission electron microscope at 120 kV acceleration voltage equipped with a bottom mounted Ceta camera using the Maps software for automatic image acquisition (Thermo Fischer Scientific, Eindhoven, The Netherlands).

Automatic image acquisition with Maps software and image tiles stitched also with the same software. 

Image dimensions: 
7471-ec-02-sa-01-sc-01-i2_OK_cells_not_treated.zarr 
Total physical size: 120.322 um x 106.859 um (146432 px x 130048 px). Single tile size: 3365.7 nm x 3365.7 nm (4096 px x 4096 px). Pixel size: 0.822 nm. 

7471-ec-04-sa-01-sc-01-i3_OK_cells_treated_deferasirox.zarr
Total physical size: 138.833 um x 156.502 um (168960 px x 190464 px). Single tile size: 3365.7 nm x 3365.7 nm (4096 px x 4096 px). Pixel size: 0.822 nm. 


Images converted to ome-zarr with custom written python code written by Rafael Camacho, Centre for Cellular Imaging, Universitry of Gothenburg, Sweden in collaboration with Flurin Sturzenegger, Center for Microscopy and Image Analysis, University of Zurich, Switzerland. An example Jupyter notebook can be found on https://github.com/ZMB-UZH/ome-zarr-converters.

""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Talos 120 transmission electron microscope at 120 kV acceleration voltage equipped with a bottom mounted Ceta camera using the Maps software for automatic image acquisition (Thermo Fischer Scientific, Eindhoven, The Netherlands)." ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000256 ;
    schema1:name "Electron microscopy" .

