<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1236#da9ced47-86a7-4d8b-a78d-088a7aabc36d> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """Images were acquired with a 20x 0.75 dry objective and the pixel size is 0.325 um/pixel. The entire tissue was captured via tiling. 

The Orion uses angled dichroic mirrors to capture approximately 10 nm emission bands.  The excitation laser - emission bands for each channel were:
Channel	Excitation	Emission Center	Antibody
Ch01	405	452	Hoechst
Ch02	445	486	Autofluorescence
Ch03	470	516	CD31_Argo515
Ch04	470	560	CD11c_Argo555L
Ch05	520	542	CD68_Argo535
Ch06	520	582	CD163_Argo580L
Ch07	520	672	CD20_Argo660L
Ch08	555	574	CD4_Argo572
Ch09	555	602	CD8a_Argo602
Ch10	555	628	CD45RO_Argo624
Ch11	640	664	PD-L1_Argo662
Ch12	640	688	FOXP3_Argo686
Ch13	640	722	LAG3_Argo730
Ch14	730	764	PD-1_Argo760
Ch15	730	784	Ki-67_Argo784
Ch16	730	814	CD45_Argo810 
Ch17	730	848	S100_Argo845
Ch18	730	872	Blank
Ch19	730	890	Blank

Images were processed using Rarecyte's custom algorithm, involving tile stitching, non-linear channel alignment, and spectral unmixing.  The unmixing matrix was determined using previously acquired single color controls. 
""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Rarecyte Orion" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246 ;
    schema1:name "Orion Acquisition" .

