<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1280#3fa8f90d-eefa-48b8-ab03-ad3ee2221650> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Tissue sections, frozen in O.C.T., were taken from the dorsal striatum and the lateral cortex of the cerebellum. These sections were cut using a cryostat (CM3050S, Leica Biosystems, Wetzlar, Germany). The slices were stained with primary antibodies for allograft inflammatory factor 1 (Iba1), a marker for microglia, and glial fibrillary acidic protein (GFAP), a marker for astroglial injury, followed by Alexa 488 and Alexa 647 secondary antibodies. DAPI and PSVue 550 were added and images were acquired using a Leica TCS SP8 confocal microscope (Leica Camera, Wetzlar, Germany). One image from the dorsal striatum and the lateral cortex of the cerebellum per subject was analyzed and quantified using ImageJ (version 1.53t)." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Leica TCS SP8 confocal microscope (Leica Camera, Wetzlar, Germany)" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000251 ;
    schema1:name "Image acquisition 1" .

