<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1292#2b9a3abd-3a22-4927-be4f-45ae8b393c92> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """5 µl of the samples were mounted using antifade solution (ProLong® Diamond Antifade Mountant, Thermo Fisher Scientific, Darmstadt, Germany). The samples were air-dried for 48 h in the dark and stored at 4 °C until microscopical analysis. For the image acquisition, a DMI 6000 SP8 (Leica Microsystems was used microscope, with an 93× HCX Plan Apo 1.4 glycerol objective was used. Images were acquired with a sequential scan using the following laser configuration
405nm (Em 415-584 nm), 495nm (Em 500-580 nm), 620 nm (Em 680-730 nm). Excitation at 405 nm (Ch0) was used for measuring intensities of ALEXA 405 labelled modified cyanopeptides, excitation at 495 nm (Ch1) was used for measuring intensities of ALEXA 488 labelled modified cyanopeptides and BODIPY 505/515 labelled lipids, while excitation at 620 nm (Ch2) was used for measuring the intrinsic natural autofluorescence of the cells.

An initial set of images was taken with a digital magnification of 1.25x, while three-dimensional images were acquired at a digital magnification of 10.5x to a resolution of 50 nm per voxel in the XY axis and 150 nm at the Z axis. Confocal images were deconvolved to improve final resolution with Huygens Essential 20.04 software using the Classic Maximum Likelihood Estimation (CMLE) algorithm, according to the manufacturer’s recommendations (Science Volume Imaging BV, Hilversum, The Netherlands).
Finally, total intensities were obtained and compiled for the three RGB channels, as well as the ratios between the different channels. Specifically, the green channel (Ch1) was used to measure the labelling with ALEXA488 and BODIPY 505/515, the blue channel (Ch0) measured the labelling effect with ALEXA405, while the red channel (Ch2) was used to measure the autofluorescence (AF) of the cells. 

""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Leica Microsystems SP8 Laser Scanning Confocal Microscope" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000251 ;
    schema1:name "Cyanobacteria samples" .

