    schema1:description """Four laser lines were used for excitation: 405, 488, 561 and 647 nm with their respective filter sets.

Images were acquired by using 75% laser power and 250 ms exposure per frame. 20 frames, 0.3 µm were collected from the top to the bottom of the cell. Z-drift compensation was used to find the correct starting plane in every image.""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Images were acquired using a 100X silicone immersion oil objective (UPLSAPO100XS) from Olympus mounted in an Olympus IX83 microscope. The microscope was fitted with a Yokogawa CSU-W1 SoRa unit and images were captured by an ORCA-Flash 4.0 V3 digital CMOS camera or an ORCA-Fusion from Hamamatsu." ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000253 ;
    schema1:name "spinning disk confocal microscopy" .

