<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1294#a07f8969-c75e-4b01-a4cb-ef401eaedf92> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """Multicolor images were acquired for DAPI (λex = 405 nm, λem = 445±23 nm), Alexa Fluor 488 (λex = 488 nm, λem = 521±19 nm), ATTO 550 (λex = 561 nm, λem = 594±21.5 nm), Alexa Fluor 647 (λex = 637 nm, λem = 685±23.5 nm) and Alexa Fluor 750 (λex = 730 nm, λem = 809±45 nm). All images were recorded in Imaris format at 16-bit depth and with 1024x1024 pixels dimensions (pixel size: 0.217 μm or 0.1204 um) using an iXon Ultra 888 EM-CCD camera. Tiles were recorded as z-stack of 10 um thickness with a step size of 0.4 um (26 frames) and with 10% overlap. Samples were imaged in PBS.

Acquisition order and channel-gene combination (all replicates): 730 nm for CXCL3, 637 nm for CXCL8, 561 nm for CXCL2, 488 nm for CXCL1, 405 nm for cell nuclei (DAPI).""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Andor Dragonfly 505 spinning disk confocal unit equipped with a Nikon Ti2-E inverted microscope and a Plan Apo 60x/1.40 oil objective (Rep1-2) or a 100x CFI SR HP Plan Apochromat Lambda S silicone immersion objective (Rep3). " ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246,
        obo:FBbi_00000251,
        obo:FBbi_00000253 ;
    schema1:name "padFISH for CXCL coexpression" .

