<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1299#639158db-e881-4622-a44e-404230db80d1> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """Immunofluorescence images were captured using Olympus FV3000 confocal microscope with 20x magnification setting on the Olympus 20x/0.3 air objective. The 355 nm laser, 488 nm laser, 561 nm laser and 647 nm laser were used to image co-immunofluorescence tissue and organoids. 
Immunofluorescence images were captured using Olympus EVIDENT VS200 with 20x magnification setting on the Olympus 20x/0.3 air objective. The 405 nm laser, 488 nm laser, 561 nm laser and 647 nm laser were used to image co-immunofluorescence tissue and organoids. 
Immunofluorescence images were captured using High Content Screening System (Opera Phenix, PerkinElmer) with 10x magnification setting on the 10x/0.3 air objective. The 488 nm laser and 568 nm laser were used to observe organoids. 
Hematoxylin-eosin staining and immunohistochemistry images were captured using Scaning machine (KF-PRO-120-HI, KFBIO) with 20x magnification setting on the 20x/0.75 air objective and analyzed using KF-viewer software.
Whole-well scanning image of organoids were captured using ECLIPSE Ti2 microscope (Nikon) linked to an DS-Ri2 camera (Nikon) using 4X air objective with NIS-Elements software.

Images were processed using FV31S-SW software (Olympus)，OlyVIA （Olympus), NIS-Elements or Harmony software (version 4.9), respectively. Images were analyzed using the ImageJ software, and Photoshop (Adobe) was used to prepare the figure images.""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment """Immunofluorescence images were captured using Olympus FV3000 confocal microscope, Olympus EVIDENT VS200 or High Content Screening System (Opera Phenix, PerkinElmer). 
Hematoxylin-eosin staining and immunohistochemistry images were captures using scaning machine (KF-PRO-120-HI, KFBIO). 
Whole-well scan image data of organoids were captured using ECLIPSE Ti2 microscope (Nikon) linked to an DS-Ri2 camera (Nikon).""" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000243,
        obo:FBbi_00000251 ;
    schema1:name "BMP balances Wnt signaling via the Bcl11b-regulated NuRD complex to maintain intestinal stem cells" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1299#a85c06a1-bbb4-446d-8cd2-6b860fa4bd1c> a schema1:Organization ;
