<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1327#8b4f967d-1e9e-4881-b7f8-c2a5f4ace392> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "For timelapse imaging, an objective heating ring was used set to 30°C and phase images were collected every 1.5 min. When appropriate, YFP images were collected every 3 min. Chroma filter sets were used to acquire fluorescence images: YFP (excitation ET500/20x, dichroic T515lp, emission ET535/30m), CFP (excitation ET436/20x, dichroic T455lp, emission ET480/40 m), GFP (excitation ET470/40x, dichroic T495lpxr, emission ET525/50m) and mCherry (excitation ET560/40x, dichroic T585lp, emission ET630/75m). The microscope was controlled using NIS-Elements AR. When performing timelapse imaging, cells were imaged on 0.3% agarose pads made with PYE or M2G unless indicated. For snapshot imaging, 1% agarose pads made with PYE were used.   " ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Phase contrast and epifluorescence images were acquired on a Nikon Ti-E microscope equipped with a Perfect Focus System, a 100x Plan Apo λ 1.45 NA oil immersion objective, a motorized stage, and an Orca-Flash 4.0 V2 142 CMOS camera (Hamamatsu). " ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246 ;
    schema1:name "Imaging conditions used in: \"Coupling of cell growth modulation to asymmetric division and cell cycle regulation in Caulobacter crescentus\" by Glenn et al., 2024." .

