        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1369#8409da85-b932-4fee-b030-a01bd99f9db7>,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1369#ccef9fe3-1e8f-4681-830f-cc939734b82c> ;
    schema1:datePublished "2024-09-19" ;
    schema1:description "The diffusion properties of the membrane proteins CD86 and CTLA4 were measured at 25 °C using single-particle tracking (SPT) in U 2-OS cells stably expressing CD86-HT7, CD86-dHT7, CTLA4-HT7, or CTLA4-dHT7. For imaging of the proteins of interest for 20 s, the covalent HaloTag Ligand SiR-HTL, or the exchangeable HaloTag Ligands (xHTLs) SiR-S5, SiR-Hy5, JF585-S5, JF585-Hy4 were used at a concentration of 1 nM. The proteins of interest were also measured for 20 min using SiR-HTL, SiR-S5, or SiR-Hy5 at the same concentration. The diffusion properties of the membrane receptor EGFR were measured at 25 °C using SPT in U-2 OS cells transiently expressing the EGFR-HT7 fusion protein. The ligand SiR-S5 was used for imaging the protein of interest for 20 s or 30 min at 1 nM concentration. The diffusion of calreticulin (CalR)-HT7-KDEL was measured in U-2 OS cells stably expressing the protein of interest and targeted with 0.5 nM SiR-HTL or SiR-S5 for 20 min. " ;
    schema1:identifier "S-BIAD1369" ;
    schema1:keywords "live cell",
        "microscopy",
        "single-molecule",
        "single-particle tracking" ;
    schema1:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    schema1:name "Long-Term Single-Molecule Tracking in Living Cells using Weak-Affinity Protein Labeling " ;
    schema1:publisher <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/bioimage-archive/> ;
    schema1:size <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1369#1037e7dd-b10a-47a1-885c-1f3b2998ff1c>,
