        <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8596-0996> ;
    schema1:datePublished "2024-11-30" ;
    schema1:description "527 digital whole slide images of haematoxylin and eosin (H&E) stained tissue sections from 431 colorectal cancer patients across 3 clinical datasets (BRAF, MISSONI, and VALENTINO). The BRAF cohort is comprised of patients with BRAF V600E mutant microsatellite stable (MSS) cancers (n=165, 24m median follow-up). The MISSONI cohort is comprised of patients with microsatellite instability, with a subset receiving immunotherapy, (n=90, 24m median follow-up). The VALENTINO cohort includes patients with RAS/RAF wildtype MSS cancers who received chemotherapy and anti-EGFR therapy (n=176, 32m median follow-up). Slides are taken from both primary and metastatic sites. Slides were digitised using a Zeiss AxioScan.Z1 slide scanner (40x magnification, 0.11 µm/pixel)." ;
    schema1:identifier "S-BIAD1407" ;
    schema1:keywords "Colorectal Cancer",
        "Digital Pathology",
        "H&E",
        "Histology",
        "Metastasis",
        "Whole Slide Image" ;
    schema1:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    schema1:name "H&E Whole Slide Images of Colorectal Cancer from 3 clinically annotated datasets with 24+ months follow-up." ;
    schema1:publisher <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/bioimage-archive/> ;
    schema1:size <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1407#1037e7dd-b10a-47a1-885c-1f3b2998ff1c>,
