<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1417#7ae5d613-e26c-4f7a-9e35-cb4471b6c631> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "A custom designed DUB siRNA library consisting of four pooled oligos for each of 94 human DUBs (Qiagen) was used for the RNAi screens. For the KIFC1 immunoblotting screen, BT549 cells were seeded at 2.1 x 105 cells per 6 cm dish and 24 h later transfected with 40 nM siRNA using Lipofectamine RNAiMax (Life Technologies). 72 h after transfection, cells were lysed in hot Laemmli buffer. For the microscopy screen BT549 cells were seeded at 8 x 103 cells per well in 96-well plates and reverse transfected with 40 nM siRNA using Lipofectamine RNAiMax (Life Technologies).  72 h post-transfection, cells were fixed, stained for immunofluorescence and imaged on a Nikon Eclipse Ti microscope (CFI Super Plan Fluor ELWD ADM 20XC N.A. 0.45). For each condition, a single stitched image (6 x 6 fields of view, 7308 x 5460 pixels) was captured, and all cells were analysed for the presence of multipolar mitoses. Images were scored blind, before well numbers were matched back to the DUBs they represented in the siRNA library. The median number of cells per image was 4503, with a median of 74 mitotic cells. The same format was used for the multipolar mitosis deconvolution experiments." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Nikon eclipse" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246 ;
    schema1:name "Dub screening" .

