<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1418#ffc171bb-bebf-40ab-8159-fcc54c435a5c> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """rescence imaging of budding yeast cells were carried out on a wide-field, epifluorescence
microscope (Nikon Eclipse Ti2-E), with motorized XY-stage, 60X plan apochromat objective
(NA 1.41) and a pE4000 light source (CoolLED). Focus was maintained using an infrared-
based Perfect focus system. Z scanning was done using motorized Z-control. Z-stacks were
acquired across 7μm of the cell in steps of 0.3μm. Images were acquired with Hamamatsu Orca
Flash 4.0 camera using NIS-elements software (version 5.01).""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "NIKON TI-E2 ECLIPSE" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000243 ;
    schema1:name "Exonuclease action of replicative polymerase gamma drives damage-induced mitochondrial DNA clearance" .

