<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1425#779cafdc-5261-4a65-b183-075bc12a3943> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Microscopical analysis was performed with a Nikon (Tokyo, Japan) Eclipse Ni-U equipped with a DS-Fi2 digital camera, a Nikon Eclipse Ti2-E (Tokyo, Japan), and a Leica DMi8 microscope (Wetzlar, Germany) with an Abberior STEDYCON instrument (Abberior, Göttingen, Germany). Colocalization of two fluorescent proteins was quantified using the imaging software NIS-Elements (Nikon, Tokyo, Japan). This software determines the Pearson's correlation coefficient (PCC) and Mander's correlation coefficient (MCC). MCC ranges from 0 to 1, and PCC ranges from −1 to +1. In case of PCC, a positive value indicates a colocalization event, whereas a negative value indicates no colocalization. The higher the PCC and MCC, the better the colocalization. The PCC as well as MCC was calculated for 10 cells. Scale bars in all images represent 5 μm." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Microscopical analysis was performed with a Nikon (Tokyo, Japan) Eclipse Ni-U equipped with a DS-Fi2 digital camera, a Nikon Eclipse Ti2-E (Tokyo, Japan), and a Leica DMi8 microscope (Wetzlar, Germany) with an Abberior STEDYCON instrument (Abberior, Göttingen, Germany). " ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246 ;
    schema1:name "Image acquesition" .

