<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1458#78528731-5c0f-489c-8b56-6d16082fcc9a> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "We used an optical microscope equipped with a camera (Ti2-U, Nikon, Japan) (VTSE3S2000, VIHENT, China) to observe and record the condition of RBCs passing through the chip, the eyepiece selection magnification of the microscope was 10×, the objective magnification was 40×, and the camera captured brightfield images with 2736×1824 pixels. The field of view of the microscope is placed at the intersection of the microfluidic channel and the ITO electrode, where the capture and stretching of RBCs can be recorded, and the images are recorded using the VistarImage4.0 software adapted to the camera." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "An optical microscope (Ti2-U, Nikon, Japan) equipped with a camera (VTSE3S2000, VIHENT, China) was used to observe and record the condition of cells inside the chip." ;
    schema1:name "Ti2-U, Nikon Microscopy" .

