<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1479#ed9d2658-bb83-464f-9a9c-f65717a2ccd3> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """Confocal imaging
Confocal imaging was conducted with a Zeiss LSM 780 NLO CLSM (Jena, Germany), or Leica SP8X (Mannheim, Germany) and frame acquisition with the proper excitation wavelengths. Maximum intensity projections are presented. In vivo imaging was at 1-hour intervals for 12 hours using a Zeiss CD7/CLSM900 microscope (Jena, Germany) to enhance resolution with the proper excitation wavelengths.

Light sheet confocal imaging
Images were acquired at hourly intervals using a Zeiss LS7 light sheet microscope (Jena, Germany) with 5x/0.1 illumination optics and the laser set at the proper excitation wavelength. z stack images were acquired at 1 or 2 μm intervals.

Histological analysis
Slides were scanned using TissueGnostics TissueFaxs (Germany).""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment """Zeiss LSM 780 NLO CLSM
Leica SP8X
Zeiss CD7/CLSM900
Zeiss LS7 light sheet microscope
TissueGnostics TissueFaxs""" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000251 ;
    schema1:name "Light microscopy" .

