<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1480#a4c363af-c43d-49bc-8229-2a4fc35704bc> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """Samples were imaged using a Leica TCS SP5 inverted microscope. The following parameters were used as a starting point in each imaging session:

Argon Laser -> 30%
Objective -> 63X, 1.4, OIL
Frequency -> 600Hz
Average from frame -> 2 
Pixel resolution -> 1024x1024
DNA FISH Laser -> 633 laser, 40% 
FISH PMT -> PMT4, 644-725nm, 792,9V
BRD4 Laser -> 488 (for IKZF1 Day 0 samples only)/561, 15%
BRD4 PMT -> PMT 3, 501-572nm (for IKZF1 Day 0 samples only)/574-636nm, 753,1V/736,4V
DAPI Laser -> 405 UV laser, 12%
DAPI PMT -> PMT1, 417-484nm, 618,8 gain

Please note that in certain instances, the intensity of the lasers was adjusted, as DNA-FISH probes were made in-house, and the efficiency of antibody staining was subject to changes. Thus, images between experiments were NOT compared in any way in our manuscript. Images were processed and normalized internally using a custom R-script deposited with the source image files. For the complete metadata associated with each experiment, please refer to the metadata information stored in the .lif files. 
""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Leica SP5 inverted" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000251 ;
    schema1:name "DNA-FISH AND BRD4 immunostaining" .

