<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1557#96ab8415-8657-4bab-a500-a69446560923> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Imaging of the hypocotyls of intact and grafted Nb/At and Nb/Nb plants was conducted on an Olympus FV3000 (Tokyo, Japan) with UPLXAPO x20 Objective. A 488-nm excitation laser and a collection emission spectrum of 487–530 nm were used for GFP fluorescence detection. A 561 nm excitation laser and collection emission spectrum 574–602 nm were used for RFP fluorescence detection. Maximum intensity projection (MIP) images were acquired from z-stack images composed of 25 steps (the step intervals: Nb/At: 2.5 µm; Nb/Nb: 5.0 µm) using cellSens FV software (Olympus, Tokyo, Japan). Imaging of the hypocotyls of intact and grafted At/At plants was conducted on a Carl Zeiss LSM880 (Oberkochen, Germany) with Objective Plan-Apochromat 20x/0.8. A 488-nm excitation laser and a collection emission spectrum of 493–598 nm was used for GFP fluorescence detection. MIP images were acquired from z-stack images composed of 35 steps (the step intervals: At/At: 3.0 µm) among the observed z-stacks using ZEN lite softaware (Carl Zeiss, Oberkochen, Germany). " ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Olympus FV3000 and Carl Zeiss LSM880" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000251 ;
    schema1:name "Confocal microscopy " .

