<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1582#b2c4c995-a898-40df-a897-3cc423d31cec> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """3-5 days after slice preparation the SCN slices were transferred to glass bottom imaging dishes containing recording media and sealed with silicone grease.
The stage of the microscope was maintained at 37oC throughout the recording.
A 10x apochromat objective was used to acquire the images.
mVenus fluorescence was acquired using the 514 laser at 20% power
mRuby3 fluorescence was acquired using the 568 laser at 20% power
Images were acquired using 4x averaging, frame size of 1024x1024 pixels, every 30 minutes. 
  
""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Zeiss LSM880" ;
