<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1612#1966b4b6-b5cf-4abc-af59-498a03e1c67f> a schema1:Organization ;
    schema1:name "Laboratorio Nacional de Microscopía Avanzada, Instituto de Biotecnología, UNAM, Cuernavaca, Morelos, Mexico" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1612#38c93698-3f3d-4ca8-845c-edb7cd15b8a2> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """A 60×/1.3 NA oil immersion objective (Olympus UPLSAPO 60X S) was used, with a 3.5× zoom, resulting in a pixel size of 59 nm. Fluorescence excitation was achieved using alternating laser lines at 405 nm, 543 nm, and 650 nm. Emission wavelengths were captured using bandpass filters: 430–470 nm for the blue channel, 560–620 nm for the green channel, and 655–755 nm for the red channel. Photomultiplier tube (PMT) detectors were used, with gain set at 1000 and voltages of 525 V (blue channel), 605 V (green channel), and 665 V (red channel), respectively. The pinhole diameter was set to 1 Airy Unit for all channels, ensuring optimal optical sectioning and resolution.
The data collected were saved in Olympus OIB format using the FluoView FV10-ASW 04.02.03.06 v4.2b software (Olympus Corporation, Tokyo, Japan).""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Confocal images were acquired using an Olympus FV1000 confocal laser scanning microscope at the Laboratorio Nacional de Microscopía Avanzada, located at the Instituto de Biotecnología, UNAM. Images were collected using a 60×/1.3 NA (oil immersion) objective with a 3.5× zoom, corresponding to a pixel size of 59 nm. Fluorescence excitation was performed by alternating laser line illumination at 405, 543, and 650 nm." ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000251 ;
    schema1:name "Confocal Imaging" .

