<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1623> a schema1:Dataset ;
    dwciri:measurementMethod obo:FBbi_00000243,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1623#f3afea15-130f-4ed3-9d78-b1328d898f64> ;
    schema1:about obo:NCBITaxon_9606,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1623#1977c0ce-0d58-4a7f-8d2e-c44c4e1f6fdd> ;
    schema1:author <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6973-9167>,
        <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4569-1493>,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1623#0d56ede1-7d4b-4836-a0f0-7a473de2ba11>,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1623#6cb709a2-0ba3-403e-99fb-3698600a0625> ;
    schema1:datePublished "2025-02-06" ;
    schema1:description """Remoscope is a label-free imaging cytometer which was developed at the CZ Biohub SF and has been field-deployed in Tororo, Uganda to assess its efficacy at detecting Plasmodium falciparum parasites in whole human blood. Remoscope images blood without fixation or staining, i.e using a label-free imaging modality. This dataset comprises ~14TB of image data collected on Remoscope.

The image data consists of:
1. Clinical data from Tororo, Uganda. This includes data from healthy participants and participants with parasite loads varying from below 1 parasite/uL up to ~600,000 parasites/uL.
2. Cultured Plasmodium falciparum data (including a titration series, images of CQ treated parasites, and a life stage time course)
3. Known healthy donor samples from a non-endemic region
4. Synthetic images generated using combinations of thumbnails taken from the above three sets

Additionally, human annotation of cultured and clinical parasites were done to a train an object detection model. These annotation labels are provided as well (under the `labels` and `synthetic_data` folders). These labels follow YOLO-format. There are an additional set of identical labels under folders called `labels_plus` which have one additional column at the end, denoting whether the given label was machine-generated (using the result from the object detection model after it had been trained) or whether that label was human-verified.""" ;
    schema1:identifier "S-BIAD1623" ;
    schema1:keywords "Label-free",
        "Malaria",
        "Plasmodium falciparum" ;
    schema1:license "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/" ;
    schema1:name "Remoscope label-free images of live P. Falciparum in whole human blood, cultured and clinical samples" ;
    schema1:publisher <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/bioimage-archive/> ;
    schema1:size <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1623#1037e7dd-b10a-47a1-885c-1f3b2998ff1c>,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1623#480bb0bc-db43-46e5-88ae-071380b9d63c> .

