    schema1:datePublished "2025-02-13" ;
    schema1:description "Immunofluorescence images from 640 Jump-In T-REx HEK293 cell lines (RRID:CVCL_YL74), each containing an inducible Strep-HA tagged, codon-optimized SLC gene. Transgene expression was induced via doxycycline treatment. The overall signal of SLC-HA channel as well as its distribution within the cells provides insights on the success of overexpressing the targeted SLC. Using various markers, a detection of an overlap or similarity of patterns between SLC-HA signal and any of the stained cellular compartments provides insights on the subcellular localization of the overexpressed target protein." ;
    schema1:identifier "S-BIAD1630" ;
    schema1:keywords "HAtag",
        "HEK293",
        "RESOLUTE",
        "SLC",
        "Solute Carrier",
        "subcellular localization" ;
    schema1:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    schema1:name "Immunofluorescence imaging of human Solute Carrier (SLC) overexpression cell lines." ;
    schema1:publisher <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/bioimage-archive/> ;
    schema1:size <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1630#1037e7dd-b10a-47a1-885c-1f3b2998ff1c>,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1630#480bb0bc-db43-46e5-88ae-071380b9d63c> .

