<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1630#6376b4d8-f3b6-41c7-a06c-1d9f964dd0ec> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Two sets of images were generated: (1) 20x for whole well view, expression efficiency, and leakiness determination. (2) 60x water immersion high resolution images for determination of subcellular localization of HA-tagged SLC proteins. 20x magnification images were recorded using an Olympus UPLSAPO 20X NA 0.75 axial resolution 1.3 µm lateral resolution 0.34 µm, field of view 830 µm x 700 µm at 3 z-slices merged into one by maximum intensity projection and 9 fields per well. Exposure times were adjusted so that unstained cell background becomes visible and no overexposure is encountered. 60x high quality images were recorded using an Olympus UPLSAPO 60XW water immersion objective: NA 1.2, axial resolution of 0.58 µm, lateral resolution of 0.213µm, field of view 276 µm x 233 µm, 4-5 zstacks, z-distance 1.25µm, 8 fields, 4 channels. Exposure times were adjusted so that unstained cell background becomes visible and no overexposure is encountered." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Yokogawa CV7000" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246 ;
    schema1:name "Image acquisition" .

