<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1661#7dc0014a-9584-4274-add7-7b3d3a9be50d> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """1. DESI-MSI: The Xevo G2-XS Q-ToF equipped with a DESI-XS ion source and heated transfer line (Waters, Milford USA) was operated at 20,000 resolving power in negative ionization mode between m/z 50–1200. A solvent mixture of 98% methanol and 2% water was delivered at 2 µL/min and nebulized with nitrogen at a backpressure of 1 bar. Spatial resolution was set at 20×20 µm at 10 scans/sec. The heated transfer line temperature was set to maintain 450 oC and ion source 150 oC.

2. Zeiss Axio Z1 Scanner - FL images -PostDESI images - NucBlue (DAPI Channel), Ki67 (FITC Channel), CD45 (Cy3 Channel), CD105 (Cy5 Channel) and PanCK (Alexa Fluor 750 channel).
Zeiss Axio Z1 Scanner - FL images - FFPE- HOECHST (DAPI Channel), CD45 (FITC Channel), Vimentin (Cy3 Channel), P53DO1 (Cy5 Channel).
Zeiss Axio Z1 Scanner - FL images - FFPE - HOECHST (DAPI Channel), Ki67 (FITC Channel), CD45 (Cy3 Channel), CD105 (Cy5 Channel) and PanCK (Alexa Fluor 750 channel).
Immune Panel:
Zeiss Axio Z1 Scanner - FL images - FFPE- HOECHST (DAPI Channel), CD20 (AF488 Channel), CD3 (AF555 Channel)
Zeiss Axio Z1 Scanner - FL images - FFPE- HOECHST (DAPI Channel), CD68 (FITC Channel), CD56 (Cy3 Channel), CD11B (Cy5 Channel).
Zeiss Axio Z1 Scanner - FL images - FFPE- HOECHST (DAPI Channel), RCK(AF555)

3. Zeiss Axio Z1 Scanner – Brightfield images – FFPE and Snap-frozen – Haematoxylin, ICOS (DAB)
""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment """1. DESI-MSI - Xevo G2-XS Q-ToF equipped with a DESI-XS ion source and heated transfer line (Waters, Milford USA)
2. Zeiss Axio Z1 scanner""" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000243,
        obo:FBbi_00000246 ;
    schema1:name "Mass Spectrometry Imaging, H&E and mIF" .

