<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1697#c179a7d9-3d1b-44f9-aace-9eac57591b82> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "For time-lapse imaging experiments, samples were prepared using the same method except that incubation with Lysotracker Red (Thermo Fisher Scientific) was typically excluded unless compartment acidification was being assessed. Time-lapse imaging was conducted using the DeltaVision Elite wide-field fluorescence deconvolution microscope (GE Healthcare Life Sciences) using identical methods to those described above with the following exceptions. Firstly, auxillary magnification was not utilised, in order to reduce the effects of cell/tissue drift over time, except for the control, rosy-RNAi cell in Movie S1. Secondly, whilst z-stacks of entire cells were acquired for time-lapse imaging experiments, for all but Movie S2, the z-distance between individual slices was increased from 0.2 m to between 0.5 um and 0.8 um to limit photobleaching and phototoxicity. The gap between timepoints during these experiments was 60 seconds for all videos shown here except Movie S2, where the time interval was 90 seconds; additional videos were acquired with gaps of up to 120 seconds between frames. " ;
    schema1:labEquipment "DeltaVision Elite wide-field fluorescence deconvolution microscope" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246 ;
    schema1:name "Real-time live-cell wide-field fluorescence imaging" .

