    schema1:description "Z-stack images of the whole neurosphere were acquired using an inverted confocal laser scanning microscope (Zeiss LSM 980) equipped with a Plan-Apochromat 20x/0.8 M27 objective (zoom 0.6). Z-stacks were acquired with 750 nm steps. To account for reduced intensity in deeper planes, an Auto Z Brightness Correction has been used." ;
