<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1851#71735d98-b4ad-4dab-a761-e69ca478b6df> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Prior to imaging, plates stored at 4°C were left for at least 20 min at room temperature, and then centrifuged at 500 rpm for 10 min to bring floating bacteria to the well bottom. Images were then acquired using an automated Opera Phenix Plus High-Content Screening System (Revvity) with 63×/NA 1.15 water immersion objective in widefield mode without binning. Two imaging sequences were set up: one for the simultaneous acquisition of fluorescent markers through two different cameras, and one for the BF acquisition via a dedicated camera. In total, 50 FoVs were acquired in non-overlapping randomly chosen positions of the whole area of each well. These random positions in each well were the same on individual plates, but varied between plates. Images were acquired with exposure times of 80 ms for BF, 400 ms for FM4-64FX and 250 ms for Hoechst." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Revvity Opera Phenix Plus" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000243,
        obo:FBbi_00000246 ;
    schema1:name "Image acquisition" .

