<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1891#eac7c97d-505e-4c63-8ced-c3d4c6599f33> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """Fluorescent images were acquired with an Andor Dragonfly 200 spinning disk confocal microscope equipped with a Nikon Plan Apo 60×/1.4 oil objective. Here, z-stacks of at least six field-of-views (FOVs) of 205.8×205.8 μm were acquired for each cell line and HPA antibody combination, with pixel size of 0.1005 μm/pixel.
The 405 nm laser was used to image nuclei (DAPI), 488 nm laser was used to image Alexa488-2nd Antibody agains HPA primary antibodies, the 561 nm laser was used to image a-tubulin through anti-mouse IgG-Alexa555 and anti-a-tubulin (DM1A, mouse, Ab7291), and the 647 nm laster was used to image ER through anti-chicken IgY-Alexa647 and anti-calreticulin (poly, chicken, Ab2908).""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Andor Dragonfly 200 spinning disk confocal microscope" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246,
        obo:FBbi_00000251 ;
    schema1:name "Fluorescence image acquisition" .

