        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1900#b67c7b99-e57b-40ec-a269-2e0abca14a5a> ;
    schema1:about obo:NCBITaxon_9606,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1900#258b0c18-c76e-471f-806c-6f94f1ed81dd>,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1900#2ded3b31-5269-4ecc-aba1-78013fd91638>,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1900#882aadbd-ebe1-40e8-94f7-d11fb52867f1> ;
    schema1:author <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1900#139eb3d0-c87d-46c9-ac44-42bb54ee186e>,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1900#7d8c4404-c7d5-4456-9cdb-6cacf7ecdd92>,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1900#959a6e09-922d-4822-a520-d8bf1dbc655b> ;
    schema1:datePublished "2025-05-05" ;
    schema1:description "We benchmarked five advanced spatial transcriptomics (ST) platforms: Stereo-seq v1.3, Visium HD FF, Visium HD FFPE, CosMx 6K, and Xenium 5K. These platforms were selected for their high-throughput gene capture (>5,000 genes), subcellular resolution (<=2um), and commercial availability. Samples from three treatment-naive tumors (colon adenocarcinoma, hepatocellular carcinoma, and ovarian cancer) were processed into FFPE blocks, fresh frozen blocks with OCT compound, and single-cell suspensions. Serial tissue sections were generated for consistent evaluation. For ground truth datasets, we profiled proteins from adjacent sections using CODEX and performed scRNA-seq on the same samples, enabling integrative cross-modal comparisons. Note that Visium HD FF protocol became available three months after initial sample preparation, possibly resulting in RNA degradation." ;
    schema1:identifier "S-BIAD1900" ;
    schema1:keywords "solid tumor study",
        "spatial transcriptomics" ;
    schema1:license "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/" ;
    schema1:name "Systematic Benchmarking of High-Throughput Subcellular Spatial Transcriptomics Platforms" ;
    schema1:publisher <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/bioimage-archive/> ;
    schema1:size <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1900#1037e7dd-b10a-47a1-885c-1f3b2998ff1c>,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1900#480bb0bc-db43-46e5-88ae-071380b9d63c> ;
