<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1943#3a8344f1-ce7e-422e-b57e-c0dd3e67ebae> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """Fully automatic scanning of tissue slides: The device used for spectral imaging is a fully automated multispectral tissue quantitative analyzer. After cleaning the slides, they are mounted and loaded into the machine. In the program, select the fluorescence channel panel, set the single-channel automatic exposure, determine the exposure parameters, and save the settings. In the scanning program, match the scanning program for each slide, number the slides, initiate the scan, with the scanning time for a single slide approximately 10-15 minutes.
Fluorescence Result Analysis and Image Capture: Import the raw data into QuPath-0.3.2 software, subtract the background for each fluorescence channel, select the magnification, and export the single fluorescence channel images and merged fluorescence images.""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "multispectral tissue imaging system (PerkinElmer Vectra®)" ;
    schema1:name "Multiplex immunofluorescence imaging" .

