<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1990#2f623587-df7a-414d-80c2-bf4ab26ca5c6> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """Camera binning was set to 2 and single section images were acquired with a multipoint imaging script for 6-well plates (Hasle et al., 2020).
Initial images were acquired for Dendra2-Green and H2B-emiRFP703. "Post" and "end" images were acquired for both these channels and Dendra2-Red.""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Live cell imaging was performed on a Leica DMi8 widefield fluorescence microscope with Adaptive Focus outfitted with an i8 incubation chamber (Leica) with temperature (PeCon: TempController 2000-1) and gas control (Oko) and a Mosaic 3 Digital Micromirror (Andor). Images were acquired with a 20x 0.8 NA apochromatic objective (Leica) using an iXon Ultra 888 EMCCD camera (Andor) and MetaMorph v7.1.0.1.161 (Molecular Devices). " ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246 ;
    schema1:name "VCS acquisition" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1990#480bb0bc-db43-46e5-88ae-071380b9d63c> a <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/QuantitiveValue> ;
    schema1:unitCode "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000233" ;
    schema1:unitText "bytes" ;
    schema1:value 8124319487 .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD1990#4d072221-8775-4735-bcab-706b5a9bbcc1> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """Multichannel images were acquired using the tilescan function in conjunction with z-stacks of 0.44 um step size to capture the entire volume of nuclei and micronuclei across the field of view. Tilescan areas ranged from 4x4 to 20x20 with a 10% overlap and focal positioning was maintained using the focus map function.

For EGR1 and ATF3: images were acquired for 647 (gH2AX), 568 (2xRFP-NLS), 488 (EGR1 or ATF3), and 405 (DAPI) in that order.
For XCE probes: images were acquired for 568 (XCE-Orange), 488 (H3K27Ac), and 405 (DAPI) in that order. """ ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Leica DMi8 laser scanning confocal microscope using the Leica Application Suite (LAS X) software and a 40x/1.3 NA Oil APO CS objective (Leica)." ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000251 ;
    schema1:name "Confocal tile scan" .

