<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2091#a2bc7f57-1d4c-4949-9bb5-addcb9c4e103> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Mass spectrometry imaging was performed on a timsTOF fleX MALDI-QTOF instrument (Bruker Daltonics, Bremen, Germany) operated in qTOF mode with the trapped ion mobility spectrometry (TIMS) device deactivated. All data were acquired in positive ion mode over an m/z range of 700–4000. The instrument was tuned with the following global settings: MALDI Plate Offset of 30 V, Deflection 1 Delta at 70 V, Funnel 1 and Funnel 2 RF at 450 and 500 Vpp, respectively, and Multipole RF at 500 Vpp. The collision cell was configured with 10 eV collision energy and 2900 Vpp collision RF, and quadrupole transmission was achieved with an ion energy of 5 eV and a low mass cutoff of m/z 700. The focus optics were set with a transfer time of 110 $\\mu s$ and pre-pulse storage of 10 $\\mu s$. The SmartBeam 3D laser was operated at 10 kHz. Mass calibration was performed prior to acquisition using ESI-L Tune Mix (Agilent Technologies, Santa Clara, CA, USA)" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "timsTOF fleX MALDI-QTOF (Bruker Daltonics, Bremen, Germany)" ;
    schema1:name "Mass Spectrometry Imaging" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2091#b35322b9-a51e-4506-aa80-6213620917f8> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "The instrument was tuned and calibrated using the 3-Element Full Coverage Tuning Slide (Standard BioTools) to ensure that the 175Lu counts exceeded 750. Data acquisition was performed with a step size of 1 micrometer, a laser frequency of 200 Hz, and a laser energy setting of -1 dBa." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Hyperion Tissue Imager (BioTools)" ;
    schema1:name "Imaging Mass Cytometry" .

