<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2102#d08fa1a7-b26e-4af4-83bb-d7c7e709fc57> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Cleared tissues, as well as cleared cells mounted into low-gelling agarose slices, were immobilized at the bottom of a 60-mm Petri dish with a tiny drop of superglue. The dish was filled with histodenz and covered with mineral oil to avoid evaporation and thus refractive index changes during acquisitions. For optimal refractive-index homogenization, fixed samples were mounted the day before imaging. Tissue imaging was performed over a depth of 300 µm using and × 2x3 imaging mosaics." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "3D imaging was performed using a Leica TCS SP8 laser scanning confocal microscope,  equipped with a HC Fluotar L 25x/1.00 IMM (ne=1.457) MotCORR VISIR objective for cleared samples and a HC FLUOTAR L 25x/0,95 W VISIR objective for PBS acquisitions" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000251 ;
    schema1:name "confocal 3D imaging" .

