<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2120#f382e733-c456-4a1a-b69d-823467b1e402> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """Serial image acquisition was carried out using a CSLM Leica SP8 inv equipped with a FRAP module (Leica Microsystems, Germany) and an HC PL APO 63x/1.20 W motCORR CS2 objective lens. Bleaching and imaging were done over a single plane with pinhole  increased up to maximum (5.38 AU) to capture the entire nucleus. Bleaching was performed within a region-of-interest (ROI) of 2μm diameter, positioned in euchromatin, using 3-5 pulses to reach near full bleach of the signal, using the max power and full transmission of the 561nm laser. Post-bleach images were recorded using low laser intensity for sustainable acquisition, with two sequences: the first sequence of 30 images with 265ms interval captures the initial,  rapid recovery phase; the second sequence captured the slow recovery phase with 24 images with 10 sec intervals.

Two FRAP experiments were done independently and are reflected by two replicate controls H1.1-RFP(1) and H1.1-RFP(2) 
Experiment 1: H1.1-RFP(1), H1.1-R57K-RFP, H1.1-R57A-RFP
Experiment 2: H1.1-RFP(1), H1.1-6xGC-RFP, H1.1-K89R-RFP
""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "SP8 Leica Microsystems" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000366 ;
    schema1:name "Time-Lapse confocal imaging" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2122> a schema1:Dataset ;
    dwciri:measurementMethod obo:FBbi_00000251,
        obo:FBbi_00000393,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2122#09b46732-61c9-4942-8f52-549fde2a1575>,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2122#74a07137-3380-4b72-8528-1be285aee318> ;
    schema1:about obo:NCBITaxon_9606,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2122#3dee3c6c-e554-4eaf-9bfe-503645e7cd72>,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2122#fa214523-182e-44d8-9e97-b174f39652b7> ;
    schema1:author <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9410-4075> ;
    schema1:datePublished "2025-06-30" ;
    schema1:description "The RNA-binding protein eIF2A is an alternative translation initiation factor shown to drive tumor formation by facilitating translation from near-cognate initiation codons. Here, we uncover a novel function for eIF2A in regulating cell migration in a manner independent of overt control of translation. Using a melanoma cell model consisting of non-tumoral melanocytic Mel-ST cells and their metastatic counterpart obtained by H-Ras transformation, we unexpectedly find minimal effects of eIF2A depletion on translation. Interactome studies identified centrosomal proteins as major binding partners of eIF2A. We found that eIF2A co-localizes with the centrosome, enhances centrosome composition and promotes centrosome orientation during cell migration. Migration requires the C-terminal disordered region of eIF2A, involved in mRNA-binding. Interaction with mRNA, however, does not require ongoing translation. These findings reveal a new role for eIF2A in centrosome dynamics beyond its traditional function in translation. " ;
    schema1:identifier "S-BIAD2122" ;
    schema1:keywords "Centrosome",
        "Melanoma",
        "eIF2A" ;
    schema1:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    schema1:name "eIF2A regulates cell migration in a translation-independent manner" ;
    schema1:publisher <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/bioimage-archive/> ;
    schema1:size <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2122#1037e7dd-b10a-47a1-885c-1f3b2998ff1c>,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2122#480bb0bc-db43-46e5-88ae-071380b9d63c> ;
    schema1:thumbnailUrl "https://uk1s3.embassy.ebi.ac.uk/bia-integrator-data/S-BIAD2122/7cc20ab8-edbf-4cf2-9ef7-0b32b0260336/static_display_512_512.png" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2122#09b46732-61c9-4942-8f52-549fde2a1575> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Images were acquired using a C Plan-Apochromat 63x/1.4 oil immersion objective and Zeiss 1.518 refractive index (Abbe number: 45) oil immersion media. For excitation, 488 nm (PCNT or centrin), 561 nm (CSPP1), 639 nm (eIF2A) laser diodes were used. Voxel size was 44 nm x 44 nm x100 nm (zoom factor 6) and z-stacks were acquired every 130 nm, covering the complete satellite volume." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Zeiss LSM980 airyscan 2 microscope controlled by Zen Blue 3.2 software" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000393 ;
    schema1:name "Airyscan" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2122#1037e7dd-b10a-47a1-885c-1f3b2998ff1c> a <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/QuantitiveValue> ;
