<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2128#4c7ceaf5-8e06-4c7a-b48f-7316a71dc88d> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """See the paper for an extended imaging protocol. Here in short:
- Confocal microscopy of transgenic larvae: excitation of 488 nm for GFP and 561 nm for mScarlet and detected at 494-572 nm and 593-750 nm
- Label-free Raman imaging: Image with a wide range of vibrational frequencies (450 - 3100 cm-1), using forward SRS (F-SRS) and epi-CARS (E-CARS). The pump laser was tuned from 781.35 - 985.3 nm (3100 - 450 cm-1) and later specifically to 791.6, 796.9, 897.0 and 976.2 nm respectively, to excite a vibration at 2937, 2850, 1450 and 545 cm-1.
""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Leica STELLARIS 8 coherent Raman scattering confocal microscope " ;
    schema1:name "Label-free Raman imaging" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2128#f5e28ff9-743a-4cc4-bc60-9e28385aa3ef> a schema1:BioSample ;
    schema1:description "Zebrafish larvae pancreas. Transgenetic zebrafish for exocrine pancreas cell ablation via the NTR-NFP system with GFP-positive beta cells in the pancreatic islet. Wild type AB zerbafish were used for label-free imaging." ;
    schema1:name "Zebrafish transgenic line for exocrine pancreas cell ablation" ;
    schema1:taxonomicRange obo:NCBITaxon_7955 .

