<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2146#f54e2f05-06e2-4b69-b431-03e51d51458f> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """The instrument run was performed following the Xenium Analyzer User Guide CG000584 (https://www.10xgenomics.com/support/in-situ-gene-expression/documentation/instruments/xenium-analyzer/xenium-analyzer-user-guide).
The on-instrument analysis was run with Xenium Onboard Analysis with following versions:
- bone_s0: v1.9.0.
- bone_marrow_s0: v1.9.0.
- bone_marrow_s1: v1.9.0.
- brain_s0: v2.0.0.
- breast_s0: v1.3.
- breast_s1: v1.0.2.
- breast_s3: v1.0.2.
- breast_s6: v3.0.0.
- cervix_s0: v3.0.0.
- colon_s1: v1.6.0.
- colon_s2: v2.0.0.
- heart_s0: v1.9.0.
- kidney_s0: v1.5.0.
- kidney_s1: v1.5.0.
- liver_s0: v1.9.0.
- liver_s1: v1.9.0.
- lung_s1: v2.0.0.
- lung_s3: v3.0.0.
- lymph_node_s0: v3.0.0.
- ovary_s0: v2.0.0.
- ovary_s1: v3.0.0.
- pancreatic_s0: v1.6.0.
- pancreatic_s1: v2.0.0.
- pancreatic_s2: v2.0.0.
- prostate_s0: v3.0.0.
- skin_s1: v1.9.0.
- skin_s2: v1.7.0. The data were reanalyzed with Xenium Ranger to reduce false positive cells in the dermis using the xeniumranger resegment pipeline and a --dapi-filter of 400.
- skin_s3: v1.6.0.
- skin_s4: v3.0.0.
- tonsil_s0: v1.9.0.
- tonsil_s1: v1.9.0.""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Xenium Analyzer (10x Genomics instrument)" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000243,
        obo:FBbi_00000246 ;
    schema1:name "Xenium technology" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2146#fd39a4fc-2be5-4524-9eb9-b3fbfc4ebe0e> a schema1:BioSample ;
    schema1:description """
The dataset comprises 31 human Xenium FFPE sections across 16 tissue types (breast, bone, bone marrow, brain, cervix, colon, heart, kidney, liver, lung, lymph node, ovarian, pancreatic, prostate, skin, tonsil), for 22 cancerous and 9 non-cancerous patients.

More specifically, for each slide (with in order slide_id / tissue / disease or information):
- bone_s0 / bone / healthy
- bone_marrow_s0 / bone marrow / acute lymphoid leukemia
- bone_marrow_s1 / bone marrow / healthy
- brain_s0 / brain / brain cancer (glioblastoma multiforme)
- breast_s0 / breast / breast cancer (ductal carcinoma)
- breast_s1 / breast / breast cancer (ductal carcinoma)
- breast_s3 / breast / breast cancer (lobular carcinoma)
- breast_s6 / breast / breast cancer (II-A, T1cN1MX))
- cervix_s0 / cervix / cervical cancer (III-B,T1bN1MX)
- colon_s1 / colon / colorectal cancer adenocarcinoma
- colon_s2 / colon / colorectal cancer adenocarcinoma
- heart_s0 / heart / healthy
- kidney_s0 / kidney / healthy
- kidney_s1 / kidney / papillary renal cell carcinoma (PRCC)
- liver_s0 / liver / healthy
- liver_s1 / liver / liver cancer
- lung_s1 / lung / lung cancer (NSCLC)
- lung_s3 / lung / invasive acinar adenocarcinoma (IB,T2aN0MX)
- lymph_node_s0 / lymph node / reactive lymph node (left axilla)
- ovary_s0 / ovary / ovary serous carcinoma
- ovary_s1 / ovary / ovarian papillary serous carcinoma (III-B, T3bN0MX)
- pancreatic_s0 / pancreatic / pancreatic adenocarcinoma
- pancreatic_s1 / pancreatic / pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma
- pancreatic_s2 / pancreatic / pancreatic adenocarcinoma
- prostate_s0 / prostate / prostate adenocarcinoma
- skin_s1 / skin / healthy
- skin_s2 / skin / melanoma
- skin_s3 / skin / melanoma
- skin_s4 / skin / primary dermal melanoma
- tonsil_s0 / tonsil / reactive follicular hyperplasia
- tonsil_s1 / tonsil / follicular lymphoid hyperplasia""" ;
    schema1:name "Human tissues" ;
