<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2154#c9c5f3b9-d51b-4f7e-9a8b-d789b7caaebc> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Dragonfly adopts Electron-Multiplying CCD (EMCCD) technology, which is suitable for CFSE signals with weak fluorescence intensities The CFSE and GFP fluorescence signal of cells were be detected using a 60x oil lens. Adjust the laser intensity, gain value and exposure time so that the fluorescence intensity of the brightest cell with CFSE in a single lineage does not exceed 65535 as a standard, and adjust the shooting parameters according to the actual situation for different lineages, but keep the same shooting parameters for the same lineage. The step size was set to automatic mode, generally 0.233 μm. The upper and lower z boundaries were taken as the places in the field of view where each GFP cell signal disappeared. Avoid light throughout the shooting process." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Andor Dragonfly Spinning-disk Confocol Microscopy" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000253 ;
    schema1:name "In vivo lineage tracing image acquisition" .

