<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2196> a schema1:Dataset ;
    dwciri:measurementMethod obo:FBbi_00000243,
        obo:FBbi_00000249,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2196#0ddd476f-ac6c-4ead-b89a-c2a55542be12> ;
    schema1:about obo:NCBITaxon_9606,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2196#be1e84fa-ee0a-49fc-aced-02ebc0356cf6> ;
    schema1:author <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2196#6ce675b3-d243-4e15-b8d1-b5a4840d3bc8>,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2196#7acd42c2-7107-460c-b29c-df78a3f4bf1d> ;
    schema1:datePublished "2025-07-24" ;
    schema1:description "This dataset contains 2D time-lapse microscopy recordings of primary human neutrophil granulocytes, acquired using a multi-lens imaging system (as in the ComplexEye setup, see https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-43765-3). It includes raw image data and corresponding instance segmentation masks with tracking information. The segmentations were generated by automated models and manually curated to ensure high-quality tracking. Cell identities are preserved over time via consistent label IDs. All data is provided in OME-Zarr format, following the OME-NGFF specification. The labels and raw images are stored within the same OME-Zarr file. The dataset is intended for training and benchmarking of cell tracking algorithms." ;
    schema1:identifier "S-BIAD2196" ;
    schema1:keywords "Cell Tracking" ;
    schema1:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    schema1:name "CellTrack: Benchmark dataset for 2D cell tracking" ;
    schema1:publisher <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/bioimage-archive/> ;
    schema1:size <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2196#1037e7dd-b10a-47a1-885c-1f3b2998ff1c>,
        <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2196#480bb0bc-db43-46e5-88ae-071380b9d63c> .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2196#0ddd476f-ac6c-4ead-b89a-c2a55542be12> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "After the isolation and purification of neutrophils, the custom build ComplexEye system is used to produce time-lapse videos in a high throughput manner. Therefore, neutrophils are pipetted into a 384 well plate and anomalies (air bubbles, contaminations, etc.) are induced in the well and the neutrophils and the contaminations are centrifuged to the bottom of the well for 5 minutes at 350Xg. After that, the plate is place in the ComplexEye system, that is sitting in and 37 °C 5% CO2 incubator. Now the z-axis is set by switching the wells and saving all the needed positions. Further on, for the illumination the microscope is capable to set the exposure time of every well automatically. Finally, the frame rate is set to take a picture every 8 seconds and videos are taken up to 2 hours. " ;
    schema1:labEquipment """ComplexEye; High-throughput multi-lens array microscope

See details: https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-43765-3""" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000243,
        obo:FBbi_00000249 ;
    schema1:name "Neutrophil granulocytes migration time-lapse" .

