<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2209#c77c5ce1-df7d-4a96-8c73-22b6ae542474> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Drone-based aerial imaging was conducted between 11:00 and 13:00 under stable natural illuminance within the polytunnel. A low‐cost DJI Mini 3 Pro (DJI, Shenzhen, China) equipped with an HD image sensor captured Fusarium head blight in wheat at six time points between 10 and 20 days after inoculation (DAI), with 2-day intervals. Flight altitude was maintained at 1.8 m, and the camera angle was fixed at –60° relative to the imaging platform to minimize occlusion of inoculated spikes." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "DJI Mini 3 Pro " ;
