    schema1:description """Confocal Z-stack images were acquired using a vertical spinning disc confocal microscopy system consisting of a Zeiss Axio Observer 7 microscope integrated with a Yokogawa CSU-W1-T2 spinning disk unit featuring 50 um pinholes and a VSHOM1000 excitation homogenizer (Visitron Systems), along with VisiView software (Visitron System, v4.40.14) and alpha Plan-Apochromat 100×/1.46 Oil immersion objective. A 488 nm laser was employed for GFP (excitation 488 nm, emission 500-550 nm). 
