    schema1:datePublished "2025-09-07" ;
    schema1:description "This dataset contains paired virtual whole-slide images (WSIs) and their corresponding chemically stained WSIs. Virtual staining uses deep learning to digitally reproduce the appearance of histochemical stains from label-free images, offering a non-destructive alternative to conventional staining that preserves tissue for additional analysis. In this dataset, the virtual WSIs were generated from label-free dual-excitation Photon Absorption Remote Sensing (PARS) microscopy data using the RegGAN image-to-image translation framework. Stain types include hematoxylin & eosin (H&E), Masson’s trichrome, periodic acid–Schiff (PAS), and Jones silver, spanning diverse healthy and pathological human and murine tissues. The dataset enables quantitative and qualitative evaluation of virtual staining performance, providing pixel-aligned comparisons between AI-generated stains and their real histochemical counterparts." ;
    schema1:identifier "S-BIAD2232" ;
    schema1:keywords "Deep learning",
        "Digital pathology",
        "Histochemical stains",
        "Label-free histology",
        "Non-destructive microscopy",
        "Photon Absorption Remote Sensing (PARS) microscopy",
        "UV imaging",
        "Virtual staining",
        "Whole-slide imaging (WSI)",
        "absorption microscopy " ;
    schema1:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    schema1:name "Label-Free Whole Slide Virtual Multi-Staining Using Dual-Excitation Photon Absorption Remote Sensing Microscopy" ;
    schema1:publisher <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/bioimage-archive/> ;
