<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2232#f209b1c7-5fe9-4eba-b816-f1266ccdca07> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Dual-excitation at 266 nm (pulse width 400 ps, pulse energy 163 pJ) and 355 nm (pulse width 1.5 ns, pulse energy 808 pJ) using pulsed, spatially interlaced excitation spots. The system acquires simultaneous non-radiative and radiative (autofluorescence) relaxation following absorption. A low-power 405 nm continuous-wave laser measures non-radiative relaxation via scattering changes, while radiative autofluorescence is broadly collected. System photodiodes record responses, and a high-speed digitizer captures the data. Whole-slide imaging is achieved via automated autofocus using the scattering signal and stitched mosaics (~40× equivalent resolution)." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Custom-built dual-excitation PARS laser scanning microscope with 266 nm and 355 nm pulsed lasers, low-power 405 nm continuous-wave (CW) laser for scattering measurements." ;
    schema1:name "Label-free dual-excitation Photon Absorption Remote Sensing (PARS) microscopy" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2232#fd70f175-c6d6-476b-99ba-08c4a2fc98d8> a schema1:BioSample ;
