<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2248#6e83b8a1-5115-45de-8b40-b6917936d471> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "GFP tagged proteins were immunostained with a GFP booster-AF488 excited with 488 nm and its emission detected with 400-550nm, Nup153 (AF555) was excited with 555 nm and detected with 525-720nm, endogenous TPR (AF647) was excited with 647nm and detected with 640-720nm, and DAPI was exited with 350nm and detected with 400-505nm. Full nucleus 3D imaging was acquired with the following airyscan settings: 0.2µm z-steps, dual time of 1.15 μs and a size of 0.31 μm. Airyscan image processing was applied automatically after imaging using Zeiss ZEN software (version blue 3.6) to obtain the final processed images. " ;
