<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2259#a784dd39-18ca-4598-a2a0-b174a0436512> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Cryo-fluorescence Z-stack images of lamellae were acquired with 100X objective (0.75 NA) in AiryScan mode on LSM900 (Zeiss) equipped with a cryo-stage (Linkam). A 488 nm laser was used to acquire exocyst-mNG images (channel 2). The Z-stacks were aligned with StackReg, then maximum intensity projection was done in Fiji for later correlation (channel 1). Thereafter, grids with lamellae were loaded into a Titan Krios G4 (ThermoFisher Scientific) equipped with SelectrisX energy filter and Falcon4i camera, operated with SerialEM software. Medium magnification montages of the lamellae were acquired and blended with Etomo (channel 4). Then medium-mag-montages and their corresponding fluorescence map were registered in ICY with ec-CLEMv2 plugin, so that the fluorescence signal could be used to guide the high-magnification tilt series collection. Thereafter, dose-symmetric tilt-series were acquired in SerialEM with PACE-tomo, but are not part of this dataset and are instead uploaded to EMPAIR (ID)" ;
    schema1:labEquipment """LSM900 (Zeiss) equipped with a cryo-stage (Linkam) with Zeiss EC-Epiplan-Neofluar 100x/0.75 DIC objective.
Titan Krios G4 (ThermoFisher Scientific) equipped with SelectrisX energy filter and Falcon4i camera, operated with SerialEM software.""" ;
    schema1:name "Cryo-CLEM_acquisition_methodology" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2259#ab45e6ce-12cf-4986-992b-55b3d10dad93> a schema1:BioSample ;
