<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2269#f500750a-7c33-4ade-9d40-acb6a342c44f> a schema1:BioSample ;
    schema1:description """.. Immunomonitoring study in human oncology.
The image shows a perivascular accumulation of B cells, T cells and plasma cells in a human brain tumor. These structures, also known as tertiary lymphoid structures, are sites of lymphocyte clonal expansion and plasma cell formation. The study aims to determine the clinical relevance and immunological function of tertiary lymphoid structures in human primary brain tumors.""" ;
    schema1:name "November Image 2025 Biosample" ;
    schema1:taxonomicRange obo:NCBITaxon_9606 .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2269#fa56d995-c1ba-4bfc-99f4-b1c9d120ca74> a schema1:BioSample ;
    schema1:description """.. Visualisation of microbial oil in the fungus Ustilago maydis.
The microscopic image shows yeast cells of the fungal model Ustilago maydis that produce single cell oil at nitrogen-starvation conditions. The genetically engineered cells are packed with oil droplets that were visualized by BODIPY staining. The study was conducted in the framework of the BioSC project "NextVegOil".""" ;
    schema1:name "December Image 2025 Biosample" ;
    schema1:taxonomicRange obo:NCBITaxon_5270 .

