<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2281#51754164-2adf-4eec-b6f7-c7de01aec47c> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Z-stacks were acquired with z-intervals determined by Nyquist sampling. Z-stacks of ≥12 µm thickness with 1 µm intervals were acquired, and the Extended Depth of Focus (EDF) mode was applied to process them into projection images. Maximum Intensity Projections were generated, and tiles were stitched with 15% overlap using Hoechst 33342 as reference. Images were uniformly sharpened by 20% and adjusted for contrast, brightness, and gamma using consistent LUT settings and background thresholds across groups." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Organoids were imaged on a Zeiss Spinning Disk system on an Axis-Observer.Z1 with a Yokogawa CSU-X1 and a Zeiss Axiocam 506, using automated scans of manually selected regions with a 20x/0.8 Plan-Apochromat Air Objective, or 10x/0.45 Plan-Apochromat Air Objective, or 40x/0.95 Plan-Apochromat Air Objective" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246,
        obo:FBbi_00000251,
        obo:FBbi_00000253 ;
    schema1:name "Confocal SCO Imaging" .

