<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2326#9279e869-9a73-4c7a-84d6-3041f70879bb> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Images of VGLUT1/α-synuclein or VGLUT2/α-synuclein were acquired using a Zeiss LSM 900 Airyscan microscope (Carl Zeiss Microscopy) with a 63× oil immersion objective (numerical aperture 1.4). For each animal, 6–8 images were collected from three cortical slices (n=4 mice each group). Images were acquired in 3D Airyscan mode at ≥1.8× magnification with an XY pixel size of 43 nm. Z-stacks were captured with a step size of 120 nm, yielding 35 optical sections and a total thickness of 4.08 µm. Identical microscope settings were applied to ensure consistency. Images were processed in 3D Airyscan mode using a fixed filter strength (5.5). Channel alignment was verified by inspecting for chromatic aberration, and manual corrections (1.2 pixels in the z-axis) were applied in Zeiss ZEN software." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Zeiss LSM 900 confocal microscope" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000393 ;
    schema1:name "Colocalization of VGLUT1/VGLUT2 with α-synuclein in cortical sections of mice injected with α-synuclein monomer in the striatum" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2326#95257b24-7366-405f-ad4a-1b83501c8a57> a schema1:BioSample ;
    schema1:description "Cortex. Colocalization of VGLUT1/VGLUT2 with α-synuclein in cortical sections of mice injected with α-synuclein monomer in the striatum was assessed using images acquired on a Zeiss microscope (LSM 900) and analyzed in Imaris." ;
    schema1:name "Colocalization of VGLUT1/VGLUT2 with α-synuclein in cortical sections of mice injected with α-synuclein monomer in the striatum" ;
    schema1:taxonomicRange obo:NCBITaxon_10090 .

