<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2330#a7b99f8e-c451-454a-81ca-8f9e63bdd5d9> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """IF- 100×/1.46 NA oil immersion objective lens (Zeiss) on an LSM880 confocal laser scanning microscope (Zeiss).
FRAP-63×1.4 NA oil immersion objective lens (Zeiss) on an LSM880 confocal laser scanning microscope (Zeiss).
Live cell imaging-Images were acquired every 1 min using a 60× objective lens. A series of projected images from five Z-sections at 1.5 µm intervals were analyzed. """ ;
    schema1:labEquipment """Immunofluorescence images were acquired using an LSM880 confocal laser scanning microscope (Zeiss) equipped with a Plan-Apochromat 100×/1.46 NA oil immersion objective lens.
FRAP experiments were performed on the same system using a 63×/1.4 NA Plan-Apochromat oil immersion objective lens (DIC M27) for region-of-interest bleaching.
Live-cell imaging was carried out using a CQ1 confocal quantitative image cytometer (Yokogawa).""" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246,
        obo:FBbi_00000251,
        obo:FBbi_00000366 ;
    schema1:name "Immunofluorsecence microscopy, FRAP and live cell imaging" .

