<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2344#11235ec9-9e7b-48de-ac6d-31bab73321d5> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """Two-peak autofocus in confocal mode with binning 1, Four excitation lasers (ex) with 100% laser power and emission band-pass filters (em) were used: 

Channel 1 (Hoechst 33342): ex 405 nm, em 435-480 nm, 100 ms exposure time
Channel 3 (Concanavalin A + SYTO14): ex 488 nm, em 500-550 nm, 100 ms exposure time
Channel 4 (Mitotracker): ex 640 nm, em 650-750 nm, 100 ms exposure time
Channel 5 (WGA + Phalloidin):  ex 561 nm, em 570-630 nm, 100 ms exposure time

A grid of eight by eight adjacent fields selected from the center of the well, 5 % overlap between the images. Area of the selection is 5.99 mm^2 or 56.4 %? of the total well area.  Z-stack of 5 planes were imaged, first plane at -2.0 µm, 1.5 µm distance between planes.""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "PerkinElmer Opera Phenix high-throughput spinning disc confocal microscope using Harmony 4.9 or 5.2 software, 40x water-immersion objective (NA 1.1, working distance 0.6 mm, depth of focus 1.2 μm, effective xy resolution 0.33 μm) and two Andor Zyla sCMOS cameras" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000253 ;
    schema1:name "Image-based profiling of healthy donor immune cells with Blood Cell Painting" .

