<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2348#22270bdc-85d3-4af3-a6a9-2a4d159f0bbc> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "The skeletal muscle was rapidly fixed in 2.5 % glutaraldehyde and 0.1 M cacodylate buffer for primary fixation. After rinsing with sodium phosphate buffer (PB, 100 mM, pH7.4), fixed tissues were then post-fixed with 1% osmium tetraoxide in PB. After rinsing with high-purity water, water was removed from the tissue in successive gradient washes ethanol (25%, 50%, 75%, and 95%) and embedded in epoxy resin overnight (60 °C). Ultrathin sections were cut using Leica EM UC7 and collected on carbon-coated copper grids. Staining the sections with 2 % uranyl acetate and lead citrate, and Images were taken on a Talos F200X G2 electron microscope in a double-blind manner." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "The skeletal muscle was rapidly fixed in 2.5 % glutaraldehyde and 0.1 M cacodylate buffer for primary fixation. After rinsing with sodium phosphate buffer (PB, 100 mM, pH7.4), fixed tissues were then post-fixed with 1% osmium tetraoxide in PB. After rinsing with high-purity water, water was removed from the tissue in successive gradient washes ethanol (25%, 50%, 75%, and 95%) and embedded in epoxy resin overnight (60 °C). Ultrathin sections were cut using Leica EM UC7 and collected on carbon-coated copper grids. Staining the sections with 2 % uranyl acetate and lead citrate, and Images were taken on a Talos F200X G2 electron microscope in a double-blind manner." ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000251,
        obo:FBbi_00000256 ;
    schema1:name "Immunofluorescence " .

