<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2363#6294986c-68f7-4eae-b4a8-a52471ace74b> a schema1:BioSample ;
    schema1:description "Primary human tumor tissue microarray section. This BioSample represents two human tissue microarrays (TMA1 and TMA2) comprising 72 formalin-fixed paraffin-embedded (FFPE) tumor samples from multiple cancer types, including lung, breast, liver, colorectal, esophageal, gastric, and squamous carcinomas. Each core was profiled by multiplex immunofluorescence using the Akoya PhenoCycler-Fusion (CODEX) platform to map cancer-associated fibroblast (CAF) and immune subtypes within the tumor microenvironment." ;
    schema1:name "Multiplex spatial proteomic profiling of human tumor tissues using CODEX tissue microarrays" ;
    schema1:taxonomicRange obo:NCBITaxon_9606 .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2363#9742c086-6ab1-409d-9643-a1814048e029> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Images were acquired using the Akoya PhenoCycler-Fusion platform equipped with a 20×/0.75 NA objective under standard CODEX acquisition settings. Each imaging cycle included sequential excitation at 488 nm, 550 nm, and 647 nm wavelengths, followed by barcode cleavage and rehybridization. Exposure times ranged from 50 to 200 ms per channel. Z-stack acquisition was performed at 1 µm intervals over 5–7 µm depth, and the resulting images were aligned and stitched using Akoya CODEX Processor software (v2.0)." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Akoya Biosciences PhenoCycler-Fusion (CODEX)" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246 ;
    schema1:name "Multiplex immunofluorescence imaging of human tumor tissue microarrays using Akoya PhenoCycler-Fusion (CODEX)" .

