<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2403#635eac0f-14c9-43c4-83f3-29bc88222d5d> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Image acquisition was performed on the automated wide-field FRET microscope. A 63x/1.42 NA oil immersion objective (UPLFLN40XO, Olympus) was used for all imaging. For each field of view, a multimodal acquisition protocol was executed to sequentially capture the three FRET channels (DD, DA, AA) along with a bright-field image, facilitated by the motorized excitation and emission filter wheels. Twenty to thirty non-overlapping fields were sampled per dish to ensure robust cell population statistics. The system was operated using a mercury lamp light source (Olympus HGLGPS series) for epi-illumination." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "An automated wide-field FRET microscopy system (based on Olympus IX73) equipped with a 63x/1.42 NA oil immersion objective (UPLFLN40XO, Olympus), a motorized excitation cube wheel, a motorized emission filter wheel (FW103, Thorlabs), and a sCMOS camera (Flash 4.0, Hamamatsu)." ;
    schema1:name "FRET images" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2403#649f913c-9ac2-4ab9-b6c6-734480809668> a schema1:Organization ;
