<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2418#362356d1-6889-4ceb-b066-4a4a793de90e> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Samples were imaged with 65% laser power using a 10x air objective (0.4NA) with additional 2x magnification. SiR-DNA was excited using 11.98% power, at 651 nm and emitted signal was gated at 658-780 nm. Data was captured using the HyDS2 detector. LAS Navigator was used to define the boundary of the tissue sections and build a tiled series of individual images to cover the entire section area. Tiled regions were then stitched into single images using LAS X software. To permit accumulation of sufficient photons for fitting of decay curves, a frame repeat of 5 was applied to each tile acquired and a minimum mean signal of 1000 counts was required for each tile to allow for robust lifetime fitting." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Leica Stellaris FALCON microscope" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000368 ;
    schema1:name "Image acquisition 1" .

