<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2432#e428bf53-e403-4590-9415-1030daedf184> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "The HDP includes a high-resolution VNIR camera (Headwall e-sSeries E, 400 to 1000 nm, with 923 spectral bands) integrated on a Kuka KR Quantec Pro robotic arm. The HDP has dedicated halogen illumination from two angles (Ushio J12V150WA), and top-view images of taped leaves were gathered. We used a mate gray vivid PVC board (Palight®) as the image background to reduce the reflectance from the background itself. The Headwall e-series camera was optimized to a 30 cm focal distance for image capture (30 cm from sample to camera lens). Scan rate of the Headwall VNIR e-series camera is 10 FPS, slit width is fixed at 20 µm, slit length is 10.4mm, pixel pitch 6.5 µm, focal length is set at 2.8 mm. A standard lab-calibrated non-uniformity correction was applied to image data. Before images were taken, a spectralon reflectance panel was also used as a white reference and dark reference image images were captured to calibrate the raw hyperspectral image data cube into reflectance values." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Headwall e-series" ;
    schema1:name "Image Acquisition 1" .

