<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2479#609b1174-3373-4886-b0e1-95825073f2b0> a schema1:Organization ;
    schema1:name "Uniklinikum bonn" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD2479#72ffaf2f-8780-4d27-963c-59b1e37d6b7b> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Imaging was performed using the Ultramicroscope Blaze™ (LaVision BioTec) controlled by Imspector software, with samples immersed in PBS containing 0.02% (vol/vol) sodium azide. Excitation was provided by four fiber-coupled lasers (405, 488, 561, and 638 nm) delivered through a laser beam combiner. For mesoscale imaging, dual-sided illumination was used with a light-sheet thickness of 9 µm (1/e² diameter) across all wavelengths, and detection was achieved using a 4× objective (MI PLAN 4×/0.35 NA, WD 15 mm, water-dipping cap). High-resolution imaging employed a single-sided illumination arm with a 5 µm light sheet and a 12× objective (12X/0.53 NA, WD 8.5 mm, water-dipping cap) for subcellular detail. Images were acquired using a sCMOS camera (2048 × 2048 pixels, 6.5 µm pixel size) operating in rolling shutter mode, yielding a field of view of 3328 × 3328 µm with the 4× objective." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "UltraMicroscope Blaze™" ;
    schema1:name "Core2Edge light sheet expansion microscopy" .

