<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD594#6f14d616-adbc-43f9-bb51-2850781d4d4d> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """For in vivo tissue analysis:
Images representing 6.3 μm optical slices were acquired using a Zeiss LSM 700 confocal scanning microscope with 405, 488 nm laser illumination. The same confocal acquisition settings were applied to all images taken from a single experiment. Quantification of sympathetic innervation was done by calculating integrated TH fluorescence density from multiple randomly selected images using ImageJ.

For cell culture: 
Images of axons and cell bodies were acquired using a LSM700 confocal microscope. The same acquisition settings were applied to all images taken from a single experiment and analyzed by using ZEN 2012 (black edition) software. Axon images were captured as a snapshot of a single plane, and somas were captured in ~10 μm z-stacks. Intracellular accumulation of chimeric receptors was quantified as the number of FLAG-immuno-positive punctae per cell body or axon. Neurons were visualized using the GFP signal, and FLAG signals overlapping with GFP fluorescence were defined as internal receptors. For all imaging, a minimum of 10 cell bodies or axons were analyzed per condition per experiment. Results are expressed as means ± SEM and expressed relative to the “no ligand” condition""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Zeiss LSM 700 Confocal  equipped with 405, 488, 555, and 633 nm lasers and PeCon cage incubators for live imaging" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000251 ;
    schema1:name "Confocal Imaging " .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD594#b2162743-78f2-48f4-99b1-2eedb19e1218> a schema1:Person ;
    schema1:affiliation <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD594#f2016071-9eac-4481-8d73-a7961955ecad> ;
