<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD616#80dc6304-6111-4248-8d38-de498b48cdea> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Illumination is provided by a 660 nm fiber-coupled LED (Thorlabs). This wavefront sensing camera incorporates a modified Hartmann mask that splits the incident wave front into four tilted replica wavefronts that interfere with one another. The resulting interferograms are recorded and used to recover phase gradients along two perpendicular directions, allowing for reconstruction of a phase shift map and subsequent calculation of dry mass of discrete objects within imaging fields of view (FOVs). Organoids were imaged in 96-well glass-bottom plates (Cellvis P96-1.5H-N) using a 40× objective (Nikon, NA 0.75). " ;
    schema1:labEquipment "A custom-built inverted optical microscope coupled to an off-axis quadriwave lateral shearing interferometry (QWLSI) camera (SID4BIO, Phasics, Inc.)" ;
    schema1:name "HSLCI Image Acquisition" .

