<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD629#1081ee47-c235-4cbc-9d59-919138bd42ad> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """The stained samples were scanned using a linear digital whole slide scanner with the following parameters and characteristics:
Objective type/numerical aperture (NA): 20x/0.75NA Plan Apo
Image capture magnification (per objective lens): 20x
Image resolution (μm/pixel) (per image capture magnification): 0.5/0.25 (0.5 µm per pixel is equivalent to 50,000 pixels per inch by using a 20x objective)
Illumination, scanning methods, and focus modes: Line scanning, brightfield.
Scan speed: 90 seconds for a 15 x 15 mm area of interest (AOI) at 20x magnification utilizing brightfield technique.
Throughput: Up to 50 slides per hour (Sustained high-throughput rate of 33 slides per hour)""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Leica - Aperio ScansScope AT-Turbo" ;
    schema1:name "Image Aquisition" .

