<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD633#9e84a5f6-fc44-4aa7-ae36-057a577b329b> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Fixed cells on glass coverslips were stained with an anti-alpha tubulin antibody (clone DM1A (Sigma)), and then stained with an anti-mouse Alexa488 secondary antibody (Thermo-Fisher). The coverslips were mounted on glass slides with VectaShield mountant (Vector Laboratories) containing 4′,6-diamidino-2-phenylindole (DAPI) to visualise cellular DNA. Tublin-bright cells were selected and imaged at random within a sample. 0.3um Z stacks were acquired through each field of view (around 30-60) to ensure that scattered out of focus light was collected above and below the plane of focus for downstream deconvolution." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Nikon TiE fluorescent microscope with a CFI Plan Apochromat VC 100XH oil immersion lens and 1.5x zoom lens, ORCA-Flash 4.0 Camera and illuminated by a CoolLED pE-100 system." ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246 ;
    schema1:name "Image Acquisition" .

