<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD703#de9de341-970a-4a67-96a2-ec11c0480382> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Images were acquired on a Nikon TIRF microscope at a TIRF angle of 60.18 degrees to achieve HILO illumination, an iXon Ultra 888 EMCCD camera with filter cube TRF49909-ET-561 laser bandpass filter and a 100 X oil 1.49 NA TIRF objective. Cells were imaged using a 561nm excitation laser at a power density of 10.3μW to perform two different acquisition techniques. A fast frame rate which uses a 50 Hz (20 ms frame rate) to acquire 6000 frames without intervals to measure displacement distribution and fraction bound, and a slow frame rate which uses a 2 Hz (500 ms frame rate) to acquire 500 frames without intervals to measure residence times. " ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Nikon TIRF" ;
    schema1:name "Image acquisitions" .

