<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD712#2f586303-206d-403f-915c-e74a90f4c1e7> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Images were acquired on a Zeiss 880 laser scanning confocal microscope equipped with a 32-channel multi-anode spectral detector (Carl Zeiss) in lambda mode at 8.9 nm bins (collecting wavelengths 410-695), with 63×/1.4 NA objective lens, and a 2.2× zoom. All fluorophores were excited simultaneously using 405, 458, 514, 561, and 633 nm lasers, with a 458/514/561/633 nm main beam splitter. Z-stacks and Tile series were acquired with 1.2 μm optical slices, at a scan speed of 1.90 s/frame. Live imaging was performed with stable 5% CO2 at 37◦C, and each imaging session was not longer than 1-2 hours. Images of multiply labeled cells were subjected to linear unmixing using Zen Software (Carl Zeiss) by using single fluorophore reference spectra" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Zeiss 880 laser scanning confocal microscope equipped with a 32-channel multi-anode spectral detector (Carl Zeiss)." ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000251 ;
    schema1:name "Multispectral Imaging " .

