<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD748#cdacd779-7fe9-447f-a2e0-53918847ec68> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Fixed and mounted specimens were imaged on the BZ-X810 microscope. Transfected cells were located either in the red (KIF3B) channel, if present, or in the green (KIF3A) channel. Exposure was optimized for the greatest dynamic range possible for each channel separately and then kept constant throughout the imaging session. The presence of cilia was evaluated in the infrared channel (ARL13B staining). If cilia were present, cilia were used for focusing, else focusing was done in the channel in which transfected cells had been selected. The 2.83 megapixels monochrome CCD camera chip was used to collect 14-bit TIF images using no pixel binning (Keyence setting: \"high resolution\")." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "BZ-X810 epifluorescence microscope (Keyence) equipped with a Plan Apochromate 40x, 0.95 numerical aperture (NA) objective, and four Chromas filter cubes: blue (Cat# 49028), green (Cat# 49308), red (\"mCherry\"), and infrared (Cat# 49009)." ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246 ;
    schema1:name "Epifluorescence microscopy" .

