<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD841#1e63aab7-5cb4-4224-bb53-61945acb5889> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Imaging instrument was installed according to published procedure, using an Allied Vision Goldeye G-032 Cool TEC2 camera with illumination from LU0975DLU350-S30AN03 (35 W, 975 nm laser) and LU0785D250-U70AN (25 W, 785 nm laser) Lumics laser units to record images at 14-bit depth. Illumination was adjusted to 100 mW/cm2 for 975 nm and 50 mW/cm2 for 785 mm. Excitation was provided at 975 nm for Sulfo-, Ammon-, Zwit- and PhosphoChrom7, and at 785 nm for ICG. Fluorescence images were recorded with an 1100 nm long-pass filter unless otherwise noted. Dual-channel imaging of SulfoChrom7/ICG was performed with alternating 785 nm / 975 nm excitation. Dual-channel imaging of fluorescent image/bright field image was performed with alternating laser illumination under ambient fluorescent lighting, where laser off images were used as bright field images and as background to be subtracted in the fluorescence channel." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Allied Vision Goldeye G-032 Cool TEC2 camera" ;
    schema1:name "Mouse fluorescence imaging with SWIR light" .

