<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD849#2780bbed-d82e-4bd8-9317-30def3e0ac48> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """For quantitative analysis 10 to 14 images per condition with around 50 to 150 cells were randomly taken with 20X magnification (Nikon Eclipse 90i fluorescence microscope with NIS Elements software) and the analysis performed with ImageJ.

Confocal images were taken with Nikon A1R confocal (LSM) controlled by Nikon NIS Elements interface with a Nikon Eclipse Ti-E inverted microscope using 60X magnification.	
 
To quantify NLS from CGD patient neutrophils in comparison to neutrophils from healthy individuals, cells were seeded in a concentration of 1 x 105cells per well in 24-well plates in RPMI medium. Neutrophils were stained using cell-impermeable Sytox Orange DNA dye (1 μM, Thermo Fisher) to detect NETs and cell-permeable DNA dye Syto Green (250 nM, Thermo Fisher) to determine the total number of cells. NETs/NLS were imaged at 4 h post stimulation using 20X magnification on a EVOS FL Auto Microscope (Thermo Scientific). 

Field-emission scanning electron microscopy (SEM, Carl Zeiss Merlin) with secondary electron detector at accelerating voltage of 4 kV, probe current of 120 pA and a working distance of 5.1 mm was used to aquire representative images for structural analysis.""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment """NET quantification: Nikon Eclipse 90i fluorescence microscope; for CGD patient neutrophils - EVOS FL Auto Microscope (Thermo Scientific)
Confocal microscopy: Nikon A1R confocal (LSM)
SEM: Field-emission scanning electron microscopy (Carl Zeiss Merlin)""" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246,
        obo:FBbi_00000251 ;
    schema1:name "Image acquisition" .

