<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD885#709bb0d8-6df7-4698-b96f-2de59dbefaed> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Images were acquired with optical resolution of 0.465 um/pixel. Before plating the cells, the first spot on each array was manually marked and the entire array was scanned in a DIC transmission light to assess the quality of the siRNA spots and to adjust their correct position in the centre of the acquired field. After passing this quality check, the cells were seeded in the chamber and processed as described in the previous section. The marked first siRNA spot was then re-found and the arrays were acquired with appropriate excitation and emission Zeiss filter sets (#1, 365/12 excitation - LP397 emission for Hoechst; and #38HE, 470/40 excitation  525/50 emission for Alexa Fluor 488). The Hoechst-associated fluorescence (exposure time 10 ms) was used for automated identification of the focal plane. The exposure time to record the 53BP1-associated fluorescence was 30 ms. (Note:file names contain the word dapi but Hoechst was used)." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Wide-field fluorescence microscope (Zeiss Axiovert 200) equipped with motorized stage, 20x air objective (PlanApochromat 20x/0.8), CCD camera (Coolsnap HQ, Roper Scientific) operated by Metamorph software (version 6.2r6; Molecular Devices), fluorescent light source X-Cite 120 (Exfo Photonic Solutions, Inc), and Uniblitz shutters (Vincent Associates)" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000246 ;
    schema1:name "Microscopy" .

