<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD953#f788ad45-f920-4595-b1dd-f418e9f2faeb> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """For63×/1.40 NA PL Apo CS2 oil immersion lens (Leica) HeLa chromosomes, the spectral detector settings used were PMT 410nm-560nm (405 laser), HyD2 560-633nm (552 laser), and HyD3 643-783 (638 laser).  
Pixel size was 24 nm, frame size was 1024x1024, and zoom was 7.6X. Image stacks with 0.3 μm thick z sections were acquired using immersion oil with a refractive index of 1.518. After image acquisition, Lightening deconvolution was applied to each image stack.    """ ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Confocal images were acquired on a Leica SP8 spectral confocal microscope (housed in UMass Chan’s Sanderson Center for Optical Experimentation, SCOPE; RRID: SCR_022721) equipped with a 63×/1.40 NA PL Apo CS2 oil immersion lens (Leica); 405 nM and 638 nM Diode lasers and 552 nM OPSL laser.; " ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000251 ;
    schema1:name "HeLa Chromosome Image Aquisition" .

