<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD961#adbdebff-a612-425d-b112-1355f8fd1d24> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Image data were acquired in Frame Sequential mode. Donor (mCitrine) and SiR-DNA were imaged to create a z-stack with an 8-μm z-step size, using the 515 nm laser at 40% power with a HyD-X detector (523–570 nm), and the 652 nm laser at 20% power with a HyD-X detector (digital mode, 662–710 nm), respectively. To verify protein expression levels, pre-acquisition images were taken for a single z-plane per embryo, using the 515 nm laser at 30% power for mCitrine (HyD-detector, 523–570 nm), using the 587 nm laser at 30% power for mCherry (HyD-detector, 595–640 nm) and using the 652 nm laser at 20% power laser for SiR-DNA (HyD-X detector, digital mode, 662–710 nm)." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Leica Stellaris 8 confocal microscope with white light laser, HyD-X detector, 40X 1.2 NA water-immersion objective lens" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000367 ;
    schema1:name "Intensity FRET" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD961#aef66ff8-5295-4213-afb2-95a3d4c7ae56> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Acceptor photobleaching was carried out for two z-planes on opposite ends of the z-stack. The acceptor (mCherry) was bleached using 100% 587 nm laser for 30 s. Pre- and post-bleach images were acquired with same settings as above for mCitrine and SiR-DNA, and an additional channel to monitor mCherry intensity: 30% 587 nm laser with HyD detector (595–640 nm). For intensity-based FRET, the the HyD-X detector was used in photon counting mode. For AAT− FRET Acc-Pb, the HyD-X detector was used in TauInteraction mode (Intensity, AAT and mfD value given per pixel)." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Leica Stellaris 8 confocal microscope with white light laser, HyD-X detector, 40X 1.2 NA water-immersion objective lens" ;
    schema1:name "Acceptor photobleaching (AccPB) FRET" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD961#ba25a678-04dd-4d4b-b037-bdc82d90b511> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Donor photobleaching was carried out for two z-planes on opposite ends of the z-stack. The donor (mCitrine) was bleached using the 515 nm laser at 100% power with a laser for 30 s. Pre- and post-bleach images were acquired with same settings as above for mCherry and SiR-DNA, and an additional channel to monitor mCitrine intensity: 515 nm laser at 30% power with a with HyD detector (523–570 nm)." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Leica Stellaris 8 confocal microscope with white light laser, HyD-X detector, 40X 1.2 NA water-immersion objective lens" ;
    schema1:name "Donor photobleaching SE-FRET" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD961#ec44aa41-dc64-4b63-9342-3a3d7abd5e7d> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "Image data were acquired in Frame Sequential mode. Donor (mCitrine) and SiR-DNA were imaged to create a z-stack with an 8-μm z-step size, using the 515 nm laser at 40% power with a HyD-X detector (523–570 nm), and the 652 nm laser at 20% power with a HyD-X detector (digital mode, 662–710 nm), respectively. To verify protein expression levels, pre-acquisition images were taken for a single z-plane per embryo, using the 515 nm laser at 30% power for mCitrine (HyD-detector, 523–570 nm), using the 587 nm laser at 30% power for mCherry (HyD-detector, 595–640 nm) and using the 652 nm laser at 20% power laser for SiR-DNA (HyD-X detector, digital mode, 662–710 nm). For AAT− FRET, the HyD-X detector was used in TauContrast mode (Intensity and AAT value given per pixel). " ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Leica Stellaris 8 confocal microscope with white light laser, HyD-X detector, 40X 1.2 NA water-immersion objective lens" ;
    schema1:name "Average Arrival Time (AAT) FRET" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD961#fb3aaf64-81bb-4933-9672-9b845a1f113e> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "For SE-FRET, acceptor (mCherry) and SiR-DNA were imaged to create a z-stack with an 8-μm z-step size, using the 515 nm laser at 40% power with a HyD-X detector (TauContrast mode, 595–640 nm), and 652 nm laser at 20% power with a HyD-X detector (digital mode, 662–710 nm), respectively. Pre-acquisition images were acquired as for intensity-based or AAT− FRET. " ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Leica Stellaris 8 confocal microscope with white light laser, HyD-X detector, 40X 1.2 NA water-immersion objective lens" ;
    schema1:name "Sensitied emission (SE) FRET" .

