<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD976#2e2b115e-afab-45d2-9303-25b51b28b6db> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """Perkin Elmer Ultraview Vox dual spinning disk confocal microscope, mounted on a Nikon Ti body, equipped with a Perfect Focus System was used. A 40X objective with a numerical aperture of 0.95 was used to acquire 20 z-stacks per well with 1 µm spacing . 

The following filter sets were used:
DAPI: 405 nm excitation / 470(W24) emission
PLA: 561 nm excitation / 615(W70) emission
MAP2: 640 nm excitation / 705 (W90) emission""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Spinning disk confocal microscope (UltraVIEW VoX, PerkinElmer)" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000253 ;
    schema1:name "Morphological" .

<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD976#3f7f198a-106f-4568-83cb-922b9dd8afe5> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description """Time-lapse imaging was performed on a Perkin Elmer Ultraview Vox dual spinning disk confocal microscope, mounted on a Nikon Ti body, equipped with a Perfect Focus System and a microscope incubator equilibrated at 37 °C. A 10X air objective was used to acquire a 3-minute time-lapse recording of calcium fluxes (GCaMP6f) in every well, followed by a single image of the neuronal nuclei (nls-dTomato).

The following acquisition settings were used: 
GCaMP6f: 488 nm excitation/525(W50) nm emission, 3 min @ 2 frames/sec, camera binning 2x2
Nls-dTomato: 561 nm excitation/615(W70) emission, 1 image, no camera binning""" ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Spinning disk confocal microscope (UltraVIEW VoX, PerkinElmer)" ;
    schema1:measurementTechnique obo:FBbi_00000249 ;
    schema1:name "Functional" .

