    schema1:datePublished "2024-01-08" ;
    schema1:description "Matrix assisted Laser Desorption/ Ionization Mass Spectrometry Imaging (MALDI-MSI) has emerged as a powerful analytical tool for various molecules such as small molecule metabolites (SMMs), correlating an analytes mass to charge ratio and its spatial localisation on a tissue surface. Despite the growing interest in this technique, a comprehensive SMM MALDI-imaging gallery is still lacking in literature. Here, we present a Small Molecule Metabolite MALDI imaging gallery, unveiling a comprehensive exploration into the spatial distribution of over 100 metabolites of various pathways and classes sourced from three distinct mouse tissues." ;
    schema1:identifier "S-BIAD993" ;
    schema1:keywords "Imaging",
        "MALDI-MSI",
        "Mass Spectrometry",
        "Metabolomics",
        "small molecules" ;
    schema1:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    schema1:name "Metabolite imaging in mouse organ tissues using mass spectrometry" ;
    schema1:publisher <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/bioimage-archive/> ;
    schema1:size <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD993#1037e7dd-b10a-47a1-885c-1f3b2998ff1c>,
