<https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/bioimages/studies/S-BIAD993#e75a293e-8c7e-4cd1-aa70-2bc1e2900f9f> a schema1:LabProtocol ;
    schema1:description "The 349-nm MALDI Nd:YLF laser (Explorer One, Spectra Physics, Mountain View, CA) operated at a repetition rate of 500 Hz and a pulse energy of 1-2µJ. The laser was focused to a spot size of 20μm for homogenate and 30x30µm for tissue samples. The high-pressure funnel (HPF) and low-pressure funnel (LPF) were set at 98Vpp and 75Vpp, respectively, achieved through 15% RF drive for 720 kHz and 825 kHz, respectively. The mass spectrometer operated in negative mode with AGC mode turned off, a resolution of 120,000 for m/z 200, and a set inject time of 250ms, resulting in 125 shots/pixel and approximately 3 scans/second. Instrument calibration was conducted with HESI, using a Pierce positive and negative ion calibration solution (Thermo Fisher Scientific) spiked with metabolite standards to cover the low m/z range." ;
    schema1:labEquipment "Orbitrap QExactive HF mass spectrometer (Thermo Fisher Scientific GmbH, Bremen, Germany) coupled to an elevated pressure MALDI ion source (Spectroglyph LLC, Kennewick, WA, USA)" ;
    schema1:name "MALDI data acquisition" .

